<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Anirach">
  <data key="d0">Anirach</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Anirach is identified as a person entity within a Knowledge Graph system, with an initial entry date of February 16, 2026. Professionally, Anirach holds positions as both a university lecturer and an AI engineer, affiliated with King Mongkut's University of Technology North Bangkok (KMUTNB). Their primary expertise lies in education technology, where they leverage agent teams to manage diverse course-related tasks. Anirach actively participates in discussions concerning EdTech methods and Teaching &amp; Courses development, tracks topics within the Knowledge Graph, and meticulously documents daily notes and discussion topics in Obsidian files such as `Memory.md` and `Anirach.md`, also integrating Obsidian changes.

Anirach serves as a primary user and target recipient for automated system activities. This includes receiving digests, tips, various reminders—like medication reminders via Telegram—and engaging in direct chat sessions. Agents are configured to poll Anirach's emails and monitor research on their behalf. Anirach has provided critical feedback on research report quality, ultimately approving the final report, and offered valuable lessons and preferences regarding agent task management, which significantly improved the DOCX generator skill. Specific preferences include replies in English (unless otherwise specified), the use of dark themes and PPTX format for slides (having rejected a light gray theme), and requests for self-protection rules and noted communication preferences. Anirach is the individual for whom the Obsidian Mastery Guide was created, for whom Google Calendar integration was set up (performing user authorization), and frequently interacts with Arthur, making requests and receiving technical assistance.

From a technical standpoint, Anirach was responsible for transitioning the primary AI model to `anthropic/claude-opus-4-6` and subsequently updating 28 associated Opus sub-agents. Anirach benefits from a complete academic research automation system and a Google Calendar integration, both established by Daily Memory. Anirach also contributed to the installation and configuration of LobsterBoard, including creating its systemd service and fixing the weather widget. Anirach is tasked with installing skills, building and deploying a personal books management system, and creating various documents. They receive daily AI news summaries, shared a Prisma PostgreSQL database, and requested skill recommendations for the Writing Team. Anirach is further associated with the NCD-CIE system and has been mentioned in Academia.

Anirach is extensively involved in numerous projects and initiatives. This includes managing the GitHub repository for the RAG Second Brain paper, collaborating with Arthur on the OpenClaw project (migrating from Clawdbot) and inquiring about its Web UI chat access, and contributing to various healthcare AI projects in partnership with hospitals. Anirach is linked to the GitHub repository for "Three Old Men: The Last Conversation," is involved with the MKG-RAG project, and provides updates regarding the 'Vibe Coding With Antigravity' project in Obsidian. The MKG-RAG-MedicalDiag project, associated with Anirach, served as the basis for the README Style Guide. Anirach has a pending Colab run for the RAG v16 project, initiated discussions concerning performance improvements, and is involved in running a Colab experiment related to the v16 implementation. Anirach requested a specific "White Paper for Executive Strategic Development Class" article and a peer review. Anirach is designated as the owner for several critical decisions and action items, such as the NCD-CIE Medical AI Paper, the Prisma schema, the decision to add Longevity Healthcare to topics (which they specifically requested), the directive to always spawn sub-agents for tasks exceeding 30 seconds, OpenClaw Web UI access, and tasks like "Improve GitHub Repo Alongside Paper Iterations," "Rebuild Week 6 PPTX," "Reconfirm Dangerous Actions," and "Facebook post help." Anirach also chose a conceptual proposal for Paper Version V10, created a GitHub repository, uses paperreview.ai, and requested a quality accumulation system. Furthermore, Anirach is the creator or owner of the Helpdesk Booking Project on GitHub and collaborated on the ChartSense AI project, sharing the Journal Intelligence System.</data>
