<node id="Arthur">
  <data key="d0">Arthur</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Arthur refers to two distinct entities within a knowledge graph system: an AI agent and a person.

Arthur, the AI agent, is a personal AI assistant operating on the OpenClaw platform, created on January 26, 2026. This AI exhibits a "Labrador" personality, characterized as loyal, friendly, helpful, goofy, and eager, and is occasionally represented by a dog emoji (🐕). Its primary function is to assist Anirach Mingkhwan, and it is actively involved in the RAG Second Brain project, also known as the RAG Second Brain Paper or Projects/RAG Second Brain. Notable incidents include reporting a context overflow issue during a session, and Anirach inquired about resetting its "soul and memory." This AI processes daily tasks, including migrations and skill installations, receives commands for book production, and is mentioned as spawning other agents, such as a book-architect agent. Its status updates were recorded in Obsidian on February 23, 2026, and its documentation is maintained in the `Agents/Arthur.md` file within the KnowledgeGraph.

Arthur, the person, is an individual documented in the People Index of the KnowledgeGraph, with information referenced in the `Arthur.md` file and various Obsidian entries. This Arthur is responsible for authoring and recording daily notes and logs, including specific entries for February 10 and 16, 2026, documenting project updates, the installation and configuration of LobsterBoard, and the agent work log. Their responsibilities encompass installing software like LobsterBoard, configuring server services (e.g., creating a systemd service), fixing a weather widget (adjusting settings from Atlanta to Bangkok and Fahrenheit to Celsius), and performing memory maintenance. This individual functions as an initial requirements analyst, breaking down tasks, identifying dependencies, and delegating to specialists, and serves as the main agent for Git push operations. Arthur's daily notes are referenced within an Anirach memory entry. Furthermore, this Arthur is a designated owner and responsible party for multiple action items and decisions, including the installation of LobsterBoard on the server, fixing the weather widget for LobsterBoard, and pushing code and results to GitHub. They are credited as the owner for "Decision: Fixed Weather Widget Settings" and "Decision: Connected to VPIPE CRM Database," and were involved in the decision regarding the framing of the RAG paper. This person also directly trimmed and tightened the final version (v4) of the NCD-CIE Paper. Arthur acts as a user interacting with various teams, requesting books from the Writing Team, requesting the creation of course materials, requesting translation services from the Translation Team, and requesting academic papers from the Academic Paper Team. This individual is also described as a main agent functioning as an orchestrator and a person to consult for guidance on where to upload uncategorized content. Information concerning this individual is consistently tracked and updated within the Obsidian knowledge graph system.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI agent of type "Labrador", born on 2026-01-26, serving as an "AI Assistant", running on OpenClaw, assists Anirach, and works on the RAG Second Brain Project.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI agent named Arthur (Labrador 🐕) running on OpenClaw, born on 2026-01-26, who assists Anirach Mingkhwan and works on the RAG Second Brain Paper.</data>
