<node id="Knowledge Graphs">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge Graphs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A core methodology used in the research.&lt;SEP&gt;Knowledge Graphs are a field for which relevant papers are monitored on arXiv and used as a tag for internal documents.&lt;SEP&gt;A structured representation of information, stored and queried using graph databases like Neo4j, and encoding curated medical knowledge.&lt;SEP&gt;Structured representations of entities and relationships, serving as a core technology in retrieval-augmented generation frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;Knowledge Graphs are a concept related to Machine Learning.&lt;SEP&gt;A topic related to the RAG Paper.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19a30e0d2c5e415e011c673f18e44e91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5ba34a6f8c2242b3ad5223bb88b8d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfa74887b0b129b04310a16bcbf51ffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5204e58e96ccc3f2974e3d4a25f97fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50b33eee641750b9ee67d76116f03226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f964ec5673640d8d3931bde2112365fd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772599353</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ontology">
  <data key="d0">Ontology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ontology is defined as a formal representation of knowledge, often conceptualized as a formal specification of shared conceptualization. This specification typically consists of structured vocabularies that meticulously define the relationships between various concepts within a given domain. While it is prominently used for structuring medical knowledge and outlining relationships between medical concepts relevant to research, its application is not limited to healthcare and extends to representing knowledge in any specific domain.

Furthermore, Ontology functions as a key component within a Knowledge Graph Framework, where it is recognized as a fundamental topic. This formal representation of knowledge is also increasingly utilized as a foundational element for Artificial Intelligence Large Language Models (AI-LLMs), often described as forming a "second brain" for these advanced systems. Its significance as a concept related to the formal representation of knowledge is underscored by its mention in document titles, indicating its critical role across diverse fields.&lt;SEP&gt;Ontology is a formal representation of knowledge, used in conjunction with Knowledge Graphs within the proposed system.&lt;SEP&gt;A topic or concept related to the RAG Second Brain project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19a30e0d2c5e415e011c673f18e44e91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfa74887b0b129b04310a16bcbf51ffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2af660d98585f1bf80724aaf6b78da7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afedad46832871dfd419946350d41dc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f679fb9f71f29d43c105efd0b6b3ee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416882a69b295573c1f83bc323abb20e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32855dc2dff1a004e9b91107378406a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41f4da4aa3333d646df07a062b699212&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e21cabefdcb6d0fa7ab2a9f20dedf72a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb398dea78019ec3ace40e37db2d7103</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772602175</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clinical Decision Support">
  <data key="d0">Clinical Decision Support</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Clinical Decision Support refers to a vital application domain and a general topic encompassing systems or methods specifically designed to assist healthcare professionals and clinicians in their decision-making processes. These systems primarily aim to aid in diagnostic assessments, treatment planning, and overall clinical judgments.

Often, Clinical Decision Support systems leverage advanced technological frameworks, such as a Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) framework, which serves as an external knowledge store to inform and enhance the accuracy of the assistance provided. The ChartSense AI MVP system is an example that operates within this functional type or domain, aiming to provide such decision support capabilities.

As a topic, Clinical Decision Support is recognized within a KnowledgeGraph, where it was noted on February 22, 2026, highlighting its significance as an area of study and practical application in healthcare technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Clinical Decision Support is a topic related to the ChartSense AI project, indicating its application area.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19a30e0d2c5e415e011c673f18e44e91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-209a10793a38ab9ffb1236b426b5f37a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfa74887b0b129b04310a16bcbf51ffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d09f974a7e07b869b8c3e753624d8064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34d14155767fde5f62677e73a2911e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afedad46832871dfd419946350d41dc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416882a69b295573c1f83bc323abb20e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-751be46e20df3b37bd63fa973c59464d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fbc27820764894775d4457c170c4c2f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772601562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Causal Inference">
  <data key="d0">Causal Inference</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Causal Inference refers to a set of methods specifically employed for determining cause-effect relationships from data. It is recognized as a statistical methodology designed to identify these cause-and-effect connections.

This methodology serves as a core component within the NCD-CIE project and is specifically utilized for the NCD-CIE paper. More broadly, Causal Inference functions as a core methodology within NCD. Furthermore, Causal Inference is identified as a topic within a knowledge graph, uniquely tagged as `topic:causal-inference`, and is related to the NCD-CIE project.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19a30e0d2c5e415e011c673f18e44e91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1518d5fca22e0855028336810f3633c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfa74887b0b129b04310a16bcbf51ffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5204e58e96ccc3f2974e3d4a25f97fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2af660d98585f1bf80724aaf6b78da7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6098a34f35ce55a2d1898f3895c0373f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416882a69b295573c1f83bc323abb20e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3791cd53d775e2d05817486d53cad15f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772601795</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Longevity">
  <data key="d0">Longevity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A research interest.&lt;SEP&gt;Longevity is a key topic concerning the extension of life and health.&lt;SEP&gt;A concept identified as a 'Topic' within a Knowledge Graph, with an ID of 'topic:longevity'.&lt;SEP&gt;The study of living a long life.&lt;SEP&gt;A broad concept referring to the duration of life, often studied in the context of extending healthy human lifespan.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19a30e0d2c5e415e011c673f18e44e91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce65e3ed28ee6a9ba6ab730d1a787b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b410b68f14dff444881b7052e6c8711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416882a69b295573c1f83bc323abb20e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34046874b056af12d4a0f9e5fe55895f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772609375</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biomedical AI">
  <data key="d0">Biomedical AI</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Biomedical AI is a new and emerging research area characterized by significant and growing scientific interest. This field is dedicated to the application of Artificial Intelligence (AI) methodologies within biological and medical contexts, encompassing both biomedical research and clinical practice.

The core of Biomedical AI involves utilizing AI for various purposes and applications across these domains. Its increasing relevance and the anticipated impact of AI in advancing biological and medical sciences are underscored by its recent identification and addition as a new focus in research topic updates. It is also specifically recognized as a research area under Longevity Healthcare Research.

Applications within Biomedical AI include, but are not limited to, diagnostic decision support, frequently leveraging tools such as knowledge graphs and retrieval-augmented generation. This specialized area seeks to harness AI's capabilities to drive innovation in biological understanding and medical advancements.&lt;SEP&gt;A planned research area.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomedical AI is a project focused on using artificial intelligence for biological and medical research. It is also tagged as a knowledge graph project.&lt;SEP&gt;The application of artificial intelligence for biological and medical research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19a30e0d2c5e415e011c673f18e44e91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97fe0dddb24f17a6ff26b65970479fd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40fa075485b63447273b59dcdd10fadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a1a85c141b50ecd59f3a228d81569a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76861888b327c0c03774d2fd66bfaab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76ef76bfb529eb0424bbe3db7d86acc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6403ad3df78ad1415d5338e0674cf444&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5762a88e509b59d9d8b593ccc501736f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb209bf42350b9e170471b4f0b4d8f51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a9809eefacfad853cbe9eca4de35242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a2b27b656d4020fb0b84a1e76aa64e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5204e58e96ccc3f2974e3d4a25f97fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a903be8a6a1e664f8430b600a9d758&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afedad46832871dfd419946350d41dc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baaf507a401ba4db4b25918ac4bcf203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38947b801f0bfb3b5333d1de2706ee8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34046874b056af12d4a0f9e5fe55895f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-333094d57c54def874daab5cee50712c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
