</node>
<node id="VPIPE">
  <data key="d0">VPIPE</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">VPIPE refers to a sales pipeline system and database, primarily functioning as a sales data warehouse for PPlus Company. This system is powered by PostgreSQL and is accessible via a specific host and port, requiring a username and password for authentication.

Beyond its technical function, VPIPE is also identified as a concept or system identifier within the 'VPIPE Database Query Guide'. It is associated with a specific prefix used to trigger database queries. Furthermore, VPIPE is listed as a distinct software project within the Knowledge Graph's project index.&lt;SEP&gt;A Sales Pipeline / CRM system with 80 tables that client companies use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28fc80c7abcbb7c8f3a3662eecaddd9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-089de8c66b50fe90b117698cc664f772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-558068083b50e64390babf7d3bc77da7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5204e58e96ccc3f2974e3d4a25f97fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7ea538b28ba259f1e19bcce7655c6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e693dc32490e805f9674d6004e634e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a1842d45d223d7cc6f6af6ba5662bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd5511d906f079895d9f4230f3c92969&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b2d817f88febf88e53eafe461680f9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772606242</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ChromaDB">
  <data key="d0">ChromaDB</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ChromaDB is an open-source vector database technology primarily utilized for managing and storing embeddings. It plays a crucial role in applications requiring semantic search capabilities and serves as an embedding storage component within Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines. As a database tool, it is also noted as being installed as part of "Tool Installations".

Beyond its technical definition, ChromaDB is recognized as a topic within various knowledge management contexts. It is listed in a Knowledge Graph, appears in the "Obsidian topic index", and is an entry in the "KnowledgeGraph/Topics index". In one specific instance within a knowledge graph, ChromaDB has associated metadata that classifies its type as "Topic", assigns it an ID of "topic:chromadb", and references a date of "2026-02-22".&lt;SEP&gt;A database used to configure and enable semantic search functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28fc80c7abcbb7c8f3a3662eecaddd9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c63f25617c9296922c676c76aabc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67b1aad64c74e49b536dcee4842fd95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f35dde77733200df47f357a0679f2af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5204e58e96ccc3f2974e3d4a25f97fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9d552dbbf4e38eaf2ae99c5d66e58ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-416882a69b295573c1f83bc323abb20e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baaf507a401ba4db4b25918ac4bcf203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885a7b5adc99161ceaae984f236f1fa8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772609266</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Embeddings">
  <data key="d0">Embeddings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data representations often used in machine learning for processing and similarity searches.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of data representation or service, specifically provided by OpenAI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28fc80c7abcbb7c8f3a3662eecaddd9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4652814dbdde910f7f2eb9c027d57b7</data>
