<node id="Containerization">
  <data key="d0">Containerization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Containerization is a technology concept and a process centered around packaging software into standardized units, often referred to as containers. This method is integral to modern software deployment and management, specifically enabling the efficient deployment of applications.

As a key educational topic, Containerization is thoroughly covered within the DevOps VibeCoding Course. It is specifically taught during Week 4 of the curriculum, with all relevant concepts and information detailed in the Week 4 Handout DOCX.&lt;SEP&gt;A technology concept covered in Week 4 of the DevOps VibeCoding Course.&lt;SEP&gt;A technology concept involving packaging applications and their dependencies, covered in the Week 4 handout of the DevOps VibeCoding Course.&lt;SEP&gt;A concept covered in the DevOps VibeCoding Course, encompassing technologies like Docker and Kubernetes.&lt;SEP&gt;The practice of packaging software and its dependencies into isolated units called containers.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of packaging software and its dependencies into standardized units, supported by Docker Essentials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-28fc80c7abcbb7c8f3a3662eecaddd9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36c79333e70770b079d3c8c754308f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ac41e7b815750ef350fea7e51f97d9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6e63502fbab0047799de5d96c7c2c14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb74e204c7dd87e73929acfc78b00ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f9a385ebc3487ab67289add07185a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4743c2841f2faaf7615a38d9da9db003&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d2ab36e78bbd6d8f02ab07f4895810d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7556d2839375abe7d7aeb2a5d26c89d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ced6f1879fff73f39fb228a7a586f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e0cfe9319855f7ec81ec53e34735e24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a77499fd86767b7b2628b024b4cadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f681751f508fd167c31bbe1d202056b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772609278</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Obsidian">
  <data key="d0">Obsidian</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Obsidian is a comprehensive Markdown-based software application primarily recognized as a personal knowledge management (PKM) system and a versatile note-taking platform. It functions as a central hub for organizing, storing, managing, and accessing diverse forms of knowledge and information, encompassing content management, documentation, daily logs, and action items. Its core functionality revolves around bidirectional linking, structuring information into a knowledge graph within "vaults," and supporting both individual and team-based knowledge bases, often serving as a shared resource and workbook for agent teams.

This platform efficiently handles a wide array of Markdown files, including research and project documents, general knowledge graph content (such as topics, decisions, and revisions), daily notes, work logs, and daily memory entries. It is extensively utilized for recording interactions and updates related to projects and people, managing people's profiles, saving guides, and various notes. Beyond basic management, Obsidian facilitates vault overhauls, progress review, feedback addition, content linking, writing, coding, and AI collaboration. It also manages various source documents like the "Compaction Summary File," providing context for daily notes, and hosts the structure reference for HA Thailand Standards v6.

As a pivotal source system, Obsidian is crucial for generating and storing critical content within a knowledge graph. It houses and acts as the primary source for documents such as the Knowledge Graph Index, Topic Index, `KnowledgeGraph/_index.md`, `KnowledgeGraph/Topics/GPT.md`, `KnowledgeGraph/MOC-Research.md`, `Quick-Reference.md`, and the "VPIPE Database Query Guide." It is the platform or environment where the Knowledge Graph and its associated index are maintained, updated, and hosted, serving as a source for action item documentation and various knowledge graph entries. The platform is extensible with plugins, such as the "Obsidian Git Plugin," and supports synchronization through integrations like "iPhone Obsidian sync" and GitHub. Notably, Obsidian itself is recognized as a topic within a knowledge graph, complete with a unique ID, associated tags, and a creation date, further serving as the context, environment, and source for its own index file.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5762a88e509b59d9d8b593ccc501736f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ed27af01b8224522c0df0deaa303c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-224d09e9eee7d60776394ab22d3cfd6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1b781e3e1d8f6931cf3aac3e89a4627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-554d48815662523a4566bd006ddfa93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-149d5849c02d97cb6c6d5223b309d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa45fc280386a72b3dcb6042866c05f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5e2bec605977d0f2561acafe070fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ddcd570d6b2e7e45dfe04d63a2b1dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfc992b66b079199681eb770fbe4ce47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d52207fa065044e301f9e39da68c057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efe07ef6b9827112c8ed827b7ae0cbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-237500f812903b7307cdca224b791a5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee3a108851713b074456d8eb273cef97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ead8544b47924f162b545eeb22ee7cde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf4ff18f4002c9dd0ded23a8652d579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-922139c7b43874c420a8e12267174e4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ed18955a872afc13c0739e6ec6ac846&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-089de8c66b50fe90b117698cc664f772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36bc7aa9b32e316be7bff4a8f43fad50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec31c467d15fe3c5a28ca03d1304cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-898034ffdfa1b10060569a60c6e94edc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16405385759a81e20e5b226bbba714cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eaa520657989ec2fc6405a732d52292&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d310a4043708aa267f31226740ed083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a6acf4ff121bf38f43ff721b71a701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dba786cd22db86d2c9ebb524a6edc0d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4f719cbd2b4a06b6e395856df09e63b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-177684e236b3aa2b6deb2be4c371a77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26049e62b3ff21e3c067d7512d1d7293&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0bb009da2afea369e4c821ce1e24395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb209bf42350b9e170471b4f0b4d8f51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b0e643ebc37d6e483ed820982ca193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-625b5a08676aa70ebee9d5d5c5803fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b037432a7b9144971fd46cf952d906de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ddd8b7d009ffdc6427d76e2b2c6bd38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e907075cce78e0ea06d5e60daafa4c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6be54c929385dd071c3a049be5445ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac86759c81403a13eab4bdb09f79eadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1518d5fca22e0855028336810f3633c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-558068083b50e6439