<node id="Academic Paper Team">
  <data key="d0">Academic Paper Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Academic Paper Team is a specialized entity primarily responsible for tasks related to the creation and production of academic papers. Its core mission involves generating publication-ready papers destined for various tier journals, including prestigious outlets such as PubMed, IEEE, ACM, Nature, and Science. The team also oversees and is accountable for the academic work documented within its operational logs.

This team is characterized as an agent team, with its size observed to vary across different configurations, including instances of 6, 8, and 9 agents. A specific configuration of 6 agents, dedicated to academic paper tasks, was noted as having been completed on 2026-02-07. The Academic Paper Team operates under the guidance of an overarching framework identified as "Academic/Skills-Integration" and is one of the teams led by Arthur, maintaining a dedicated focus on academic subject matter.

Furthermore, the Academic Paper Team functions as a project, officially created on 2026-02-23. This project is specifically tagged as a knowledge-graph related initiative and holds a close relation to the RAG Second Brain Paper.&lt;SEP&gt;A rigorous multi-agent system designed to produce publication-ready research papers meeting the standards of top-tier journals.&lt;SEP&gt;A team that now includes the Journal-Scout Agent and comprises 44 agents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2cf3a796b09887b7b8355de43da736f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041d128ced8892285239ffadbdd877cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baaf507a401ba4db4b25918ac4bcf203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-425c8ebad379a052e2cdc73544202aa3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-296f2856d7ea85e61339b7d5fc2466b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7540722cdec2c35b0cf85a5979b43057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16aa16294c1a8087f5e8fa6f3e8f6bc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465cfc7fed7647f14ac063c527100a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-284d2efbc11f924a38ffe2ce9455fd8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9e9ea9f9ef3e6e49b68f230ad0b56ef</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772610163</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Writing Team">
  <data key="d0">Writing Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Writing Team is a professional and autonomous group of specialized agents primarily dedicated to producing comprehensive books and various forms of technical content. Its establishment was considered a major accomplishment and is documented in a memory log, forming an integral part of a larger operational framework or setup.

While predominantly described as consisting of six core members, fulfilling specialized roles such as a book-architect, research-lead, chapter-writer, dev-editor, copy-editor, and publisher, the team's composition can be dynamic. It was initially identified with eight agents, and an account also mentioned seven. During a Major Agent Team Upgrade, the team received new agents, specifically a `Fact-Checker Agent` and an `Engagement-Analyst Agent`, illustrating its adaptable structure.

Operating in full auto mode, the Writing Team executes its responsibilities without requiring external approvals, managing the entire book production pipeline from architecture and research to writing, editing, and final publishing. Typical book outputs range from 120 to 200 pages. Beyond book production, the team is responsible for creating the AI News Digest and the novel "Three Old Men: The Last Conversation." It was also associated with the "Three Old Men - Thai Translation" project, which was completed on February 5th, 2026. Fundamentally, its focus encompasses all aspects of writing and content creation.

The Writing Team functions as one of five specific agent teams configured within a broader project. It is led by Arthur and guided by Writing/Skills-Integration. The team maintains work logs, though an entry for February 21st, 2026, reported no active sessions. Conceptually, the "Writing Team" is also understood as a project itself, tagged as both a project and a knowledge graph. Skill recommendations have been made for the team, pending confirmation for installation.&lt;SEP&gt;A professional writing team created with 6 specialized agents, responsible for tasks like book architecture, research, writing, editing, and publishing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Writing Team is a 6-agent professional team created as part of a setup, including various specialized roles.&lt;SEP&gt;A 6-agent professional writing team that was created as a major accomplishment.&lt;SEP&gt;A professional writing team created with 6 specialized agents, responsible for tasks like book architecture, research, writing, editing, and publishing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Writing Team is a 6-agent professional team created as part of a setup, including various specialized roles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2cf3a796b09887b7b8355de43da736f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-481427393c6695a98dde842249c71ce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff7e841b0e01ffce5ef55c819c75a7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0f96b3cab53fea5f500f4f1083e5008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a68fc9c7479f5ca8f832d201f36644f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fee19755a3251618ba78c3efffeb833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32dc00afb723b10d3141d9f4653b224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa3eb63b70351ba692b01c713f5ea165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73ac079dcb226ab3679810b297930c3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac42e4b444b2aa35a9817c58b1eaadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baaf507a401ba4db4b25918ac4bcf203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697c17c9e9d1440d003278e6c0653517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e50f018ab794854428e9bfc66b36eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46acd3e509aa2a1265a39d2c0a5e6f5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-296f2856d7ea85e61339b7d5fc2466b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465cfc7fed7647f14ac063c527100a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c2753f45f158b0a6204d83e9fa7880a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-570c1687de41e99a692ad24992a2accd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b7611801b56d161d9e4809cd690f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e967df27452deff8d725b325aa563ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f18c72310dfe68bd9a70bc2f54ec35b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a7e10d09f982e9b7d5bb3d226d90b24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b2d7eca9e5caaa2ebab4c11d5b308eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b394110aeea60586b9d87bbb1349ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-572bc319ace0969403b23edbb05f1603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a2f4932683deada51cf0bb651a5811&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6c15de56039236682f9856e47cab92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61736ce38c27461a2b10ba4645d7dc0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37056b34934d569bff0b96c6e8991103</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772910639</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Translation Team">
  <data key="d0">Translation Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Translation Team is identified as a specialized multi-agent system and a professional agent team primarily focused on language translation activities, particularly dedicated to providing high-quality Thai translations that read as if originally written in Thai. Its core mission involves achieving nuanced and accurate renditions through cultural adaptation, adapting cultural nuances, idioms, and style, specifically facilitating communication between English and Thai languages. Associated with knowledge graphs, the team is one of the teams led by Arthur and operates under Translation/Skills-Integration principles, emphasizing skills integration as a key aspect of its operation.

The team's operational methodology strategically incorporates translation memory and implements back-translation for quality assurance (QA). It is known to handle literary and technical translations, including book translations and chapters. The Translation Team is responsible for and manages the "Three Old Men - Thai Translation" project. Within a broader project framework, it is considered one of five specific teams of agents that have been configured.

Different configurations for the Translation Team have been noted. A principal configuration consists of 8 agents, often associated with a dedicated professional guide. A distinct, task-specific team comprising 6 agents was also set up for specific Thai translation tasks, with its completion recorded on 2026-02-07. Additionally, another configuration mentions 7 agents for translation tasks. The team received new agents, specifically a `Translation-Memory Agent` and a `Back-Translator Agent`, during a Major Agent Team Upgrade, aligning with its documented methodologies. A work log for February 21st, 2026, reported no active sessions for the Translation Team.&lt;SEP&gt;A team that received 8 new skills.&lt;SEP&gt;The Translation Team is an agent team consisting of 7 agents: translation-architect, thai-linguist, cultural-adapter, style-polisher, document-formatter, quality-reviewer, and thai-translator.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2cf3a796b09887b7b8355de43da736f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d310a4043708aa267f31226740ed083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c3bbc6161991a60ef58482f8460ddc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfa74887b0b129b04310a16bcbf51ffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac42e4b444b2aa35a9817c58b1eaadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baaf507a401ba4db4b25918ac4bcf203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab8b08a3f31a591e78612630a4834ca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e50f018ab794854428e9bfc66b36eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-296f2856d7ea85e61339b7d5fc2466b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734ec6fc710d1be198572ead525f9006&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465cfc7fed7647f14ac063c527100a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c2753f45f158b0a6204d83e9fa7880a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-570c1687de41e99a692ad24992a2accd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b7611801b56d161d9e4809cd690f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33c4187af5916e71523673ad409c8f56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a7e10d09f982e9b7d5bb3d226d90b24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba508f45949882ad8abe499c098ae8d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3b8b8b210560c10d99d3e258c99b2f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b394110aeea60586b9d87bbb1349ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-572bc319ace0969403b23edbb05f1603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a2f4932683deada51cf0bb651a5811&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6c15de56039236682f9856e47cab92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61736ce38c27461a2b10ba4645d7dc0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37056b34934d569bff0b96c6e8991103</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772609966</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Course Prep Team">
  <data key="d0">Course Prep Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Course Prep Team is an agent team primarily dedicated to course preparation tasks. It is specifically designed to generate complete course materials from minimal input. While consistently identified as an agent team, its composition has been described as comprising both 7 and 10 agents in different contexts.

This team operates under the leadership of Arthur and is guided by the principle of 'Course/Skills-Integration'. Its core responsibility involves preparing course materials, with all its activities meticulously documented in a work log. The Course Prep Team is recognized as a project within a knowledge graph and is also noted as a related topic for 'Vibe Coding With Antigravity'. One specific configuration or project phase of this team was completed on 2026-02-09.&lt;SEP&gt;The team responsible for preparing the course materials for the DevOps with VibeCoding course.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2cf3a796b09887b7b8355de43da736f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c630bb67beebd417245a9d2e9e12de8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baaf507a401ba4db4b25918ac4bcf203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc3e32fc1224192d75f088e0be90fbe8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-962708e2b38cf807f5da24a5a99fe6a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-296f2856d7ea85e61339b7d5fc2466b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465cfc7fed7647f14ac063c527100a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d713004e53905bc9678b48a899d29a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62b5576904ddba71ef0e4ad0f9e1b507</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772608146</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Coding Team">
  <data key="d0">Coding Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Coding Team functions as a multi-agent software development workflow, acting as an agent team, group, organization, or entity. It is led by Arthur and operates under the guiding principle of Coding/Skills-Integration, emphasizing the integration of various skills in its operations. Functionally, it is an implied team primarily dedicated to coding and software development tasks, and is one of five specific agent teams configured within a larger project associated with a knowledge graph.

The team is composed of eight agents and one orchestrator. Its members include roles such as a code-review agent, a PR agent, testing, documentation (docs), a UX/UI Designer Agent, DevOps, and a database specialist, in addition to the orchestrator. The Coding Team has been enhanced with various capabilities and working modes, having received nine new skills. It is fully configured with specific AI agents, including Opus and Sonnet, for different roles within its framework.

Utilizing Claude Code as its execution engine, the Coding Team is responsible for configuring specific roles and is the designated recipient for a UX/UI Designer Agent, which was added to the team. Its responsibilities also encompass receiving Experiment Design Content for the implementation of associated experiments, handling project documentation according to established conventions, and being specifically accountable for entries in the project's work log. Notable projects under its purview include the RAG Second Brain Implementation and the creation and deployment of the AI Research Dashboard. Operationally, the Coding Team completed its Claude Code execution on February 8th, 2026, and reported no active sessions in the work log as of February 21st, 2026. A Coding Manual v3 is currently in progress for this team.&lt;SEP&gt;A team whose roles were fully configured on 2026-03-01, with Opus and Sonnet assigned to specific functions.&lt;SEP&gt;A team that had a UX/UI Designer Agent added to it.&lt;SEP&gt;A team that had a UX/UI Designer Agent added to it.&lt;SEP&gt;The coding team was fully configured on 2026-03-01 with specific roles assigned to Opus and Sonnet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2cf3a796b09887b7b8355de43da736f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d395d729f7f4af176337bfefc3a79dd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c9f0047cf0851b406258ad13a0ecf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb41aa2ca304e58f55fd006f67adb483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d310a4043708aa267f31226740ed083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b037432a7b9144971fd46cf952d906de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fee19755a3251618ba78c3efffeb833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22dff12fa45dfc4789663451e530bd72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-876c9d36604a2a00ba9d1acc186c490c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4a759f0caa83cf9e50057d50a49419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baaf507a401ba4db4b25918ac4bcf203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b689f3d71dd57c707b347058466c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0cab046834069e9c764cbdfafb47ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e50f018ab794854428e9bfc66b36eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d5c4c8de43b11d9e06621d8f9f7a46a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-296f2856d7ea85e61339b7d5fc2466b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465cfc7fed7647f14ac063c527100a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c2753f45f158b0a6204d83e9fa7880a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42dbcaaa04c776c9a79e4a0a86e4077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-570c1687de41e99a692ad24992a2accd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b7611801b56d161d9e4809cd690f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d937855d6741d631206fe2166f581ce1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a77499fd86767b7b2628b024b4cadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-000e5cbc3c5b62de4af4981edce03d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e788ba3e64d85e6086e324e92e602039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0eb57ca17daeb1dd32503d612878c20c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bdd7a8ac37441f958ecd1d004dda478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c6144f7eea8f9ff2209417a52185401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b394110aeea60586b9d87bbb1349ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-572bc319ace0969403b23edbb05f1603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6c15de56039236682f9856e47cab92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61736ce38c27461a2b10ba4645d7dc0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37056b34934d569bff0b96c6e8991103&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-893f12cbfe862ebe1e62f29a7e11b350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f92681cbc13202ffab87956e20912b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-333094d57c54def874daab5cee50712c</data>
