<node id="Session Snapshot">
  <data key="d0">Session Snapshot</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A Session Snapshot is primarily defined as a specific data record or event designed to capture and preserve the state of an active session at a particular moment or specific timestamp. It functions as a comprehensive, detailed, and recorded snapshot of an active agent, user, or system session's operational status and activity. These snapshots are typically associated with an active agent session, exemplified by instances such as `agent:chapter-writer:main` or `Agent Chapter Writer Main`, and are frequently identified by a message number. They may also include specific timestamps, such as `09:31 BKK`, and are often described as being captured from a Memory Source or Memory System.

The records contained within a Session Snapshot are rich in detail. They include full message specifics, message snippets, the last message exchanged, and the source or sender of that last message. Furthermore, they log the total message count or number of messages exchanged, overall session activity, specifics about the involved agent, the session's name, the session type, other communication details, and user interaction. Essentially, a Session Snapshot captures the state, status, associated agent, and all relevant communication elements of an active session.

It is important to note an inconsistency in the understanding of a Session Snapshot. While the overwhelming majority of definitions describe it as an informational data artifact that records a session's state, one particular viewpoint identifies a Session Snapshot as a person whose activities and interactions are regularly captured and recorded. This presents a significant divergence from the collective understanding of a Session Snapshot as an informational record of a system process or state.&lt;SEP&gt;A recorded snapshot of an active agent session, detailing its status and last message source.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94a2fbefdc9f95d4468f72555b31c9af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea5150e6fca2cc266a2614914dfb7239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a96711df30e423083e5615749406cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a987e2ef6f4df602844b47725e43fa1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-865b9f607b6143b2991ea86a5c2b5170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34d4b2ec7ee0c088af57b411041ae5e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a81e082bc50b15702ab13196b65fcf7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e320e464065b3308d7db948d1e827156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90a4287e7a69589023f97fe208e724fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06fdd29b547fa50066bbf918525b3b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a062d9e10fe963a0eab42f0cb70b892&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7fa47b70626d922608669a39522b369&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-932e70986da082d91d36bf6d3f117889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f98dfd0c3dfc54b13cd9aefbd42f73d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc0b5accf865538247068fa2c8b6f4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d9fab81d1eec0211cefd1449d9763e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d5be9af31c8385a55b4042062e087f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f744c0dc9832bb7420464d649488eab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87973f7f18cf8516d82456867f60e79f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08e86d0e562a146331150d19c4c5e67c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07fc1acb7742fd80221f70cc930bc3f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0c2a9031f1b858d79f12378d220496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1804599fe5a3988c5fa6a0d70774afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3017826b5ba6932e21c407fc93f5099d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
