<node id="Restart Command">
  <data key="d0">Restart Command</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Restart Command is a specific operational instruction, consistently represented by the text snippet "/restart". This command is primarily utilized to interact with and reinitialize an agent session.

Typically, the "/restart" command is initiated by a Telegram User and transmitted within an active agent session. It is frequently documented within session snapshots, where its presence often signifies the last message received, the last message sent, or the overall content of the final message within that session. For example, it has been noted as the last message received in specific contexts, such as the Agent Chapter Writer Main Session. Its consistent appearance in session data, particularly marking the conclusion of interactions, highlights its role in session management and state resetting.&lt;SEP&gt;The "/restart" snippet, which was the last message in a session.&lt;SEP&gt;The specific command "/restart" used to interact with an agent session.&lt;SEP&gt;A command snippet "/restart" found within a session snapshot.&lt;SEP&gt;The "/restart" snippet, which was the last message in a session.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-94a2fbefdc9f95d4468f72555b31c9af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a96711df30e423083e5615749406cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-865b9f607b6143b2991ea86a5c2b5170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ee70ff66b5db6fafbda166046803fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e320e464065b3308d7db948d1e827156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1804eb6932c404a91cf48d839d40b2bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7fa47b70626d922608669a39522b369&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-932e70986da082d91d36bf6d3f117889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f98dfd0c3dfc54b13cd9aefbd42f73d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8a919f3748dda0a162989257025876c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4d5be9af31c8385a55b4042062e087f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87973f7f18cf8516d82456867f60e79f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0a4425eeb6a909ec03274c53503d906&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cd04a98c88cb9a6e7d71b7f3ad2c996</data>
