<node id="Workspaces">
  <data key="d0">Workspaces</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Workspaces are defined as dedicated digital environments or areas established for each agent belonging to the professional writing team. These environments are specifically created to enable agents to perform their assigned work tasks. Each workspace is typically associated with a distinct system path, such as `~/.openclaw/workspace-{agent-name}`, which specifies its location and structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-481427393c6695a98dde842249c71ce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff7e841b0e01ffce5ef55c819c75a7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0f96b3cab53fea5f500f4f1083e5008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa3eb63b70351ba692b01c713f5ea165</data>
