<node id="Openclaw">
  <data key="d0">Openclaw</data>
  <data key="d1">software</data>
  <data key="d2">Openclaw is described as a comprehensive system, framework, platform, or software primarily dedicated to the creation, hosting, and management of workspaces for various agents. It is specifically noted for its application in supporting professional writing team agents, serving as the foundational structure where these agent-specific workspaces are located and managed.

The system's operational presence is further indicated by its associated directory structure on a file system, with specific paths such as `~/.openclaw/` and `~/.openclaw/workspace-{agent-name}` pointing to the locations where agent workspaces reside within the Openclaw environment. Beyond its functional role in workspace management, Openclaw is also referenced in a migration decision entry, which is dated February 1, 2026.&lt;SEP&gt;Openclaw is a system or software used for creating workspaces for agents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-481427393c6695a98dde842249c71ce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6555e17adfd0ca119138f8d1204083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff7e841b0e01ffce5ef55c819c75a7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-224d09e9eee7d60776394ab22d3cfd6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cfc6c6d57918fbe9483abfa3d8a7110&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32dc00afb723b10d3141d9f4653b224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa3eb63b70351ba692b01c713f5ea165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cae40cb3e01f7f44617fe6efce540e24</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772910640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Memory Log">
  <data key="d0">Memory Log</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Memory Log is a specialized type of log entry or content primarily found within Obsidian's daily notes. It is specifically designed for recording information associated with a particular date, functioning as a comprehensive record of various aspects over time. These logs document a wide array of details, including daily activities, personal thoughts, memories, major accomplishments, significant events, ongoing updates, and progress, often encompassing technical lessons learned.

The content of Memory Logs frequently pertains to the activities and reflections of a central individual identified as Arthur. For example, specific entries illustrate their diverse scope: an entry from February 4, 2026, details the setup progress for the Bookshelf App Project; another from February 5, 2026, records major accomplishments and technical lessons; and a log entry from February 14, 2026, documents events and updates, notably including a model update for Claude Opus. Arthur is a key person entity whose involvement spans setting up teams, managing various projects, and updating models, with these actions and developments often detailed within the Memory Log entries.&lt;SEP&gt;A person entity central to the logs, involved in setting up teams, managing projects, and updating models.&lt;SEP&gt;Memory Log is a type of log entry found within Obsidian daily notes.&lt;SEP&gt;A system or record for storing chronological information, often associated with a specific date or timestamp.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dc6fcf70267592172f417dccb380b103&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-698aa50ab28f0e3566cb6e574a6621f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6555e17adfd0ca119138f8d1204083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd74135092e0a76db2ea1ed4d25f626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ff7e841b0e01ffce5ef55c819c75a7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71616aeafc61b899b58cf170dee71ae7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d3bd213694bc9e9a86ea3a0c974c0d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa45fc280386a72b3dcb6042866c05f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-efe07ef6b9827112c8ed827b7ae0cbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32dc00afb723b10d3141d9f4653b224&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8268912354c6ad40989f1deca0c0990f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ff7de3ecdbdeec06151e805c84a460f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3017826b5ba6932e21c407fc93f5099d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
