<node id="Base URL">
  <data key="d0">Base URL</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A Base URL is defined as a configuration parameter or setting that specifies the foundational web address or endpoint for an API or service. This parameter is prominently associated with the Google Embedding Provider, for which it functions as a crucial endpoint.

A specific instance of a Base URL configured for the Google Embedding Provider is "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta". This particular endpoint has undergone an update, notably changing from its previous value of "https://unused".

While primarily highlighted in the context of the Google Embedding Provider, the concept of a Base URL is also described more broadly as a specific attribute or piece of data that can be associated with other entities, such as the Anthropic Provider.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dbddb0cc8f3daa198946451856e988a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea5150e6fca2cc266a2614914dfb7239&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a96711df30e423083e5615749406cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90a4287e7a69589023f97fe208e724fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06fdd29b547fa50066bbf918525b3b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-624a958646ff967dbef13904a2c3a0ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc0b5accf865538247068fa2c8b6f4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f744c0dc9832bb7420464d649488eab</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
