<node id="Session Notes">
  <data key="d0">Session Notes</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Session Notes are defined as detailed records, documents, or a set of notes typically associated with specific dates or work sessions. Their primary purpose is to document extensive work performed across multiple projects.

These notes contain various types of information crucial for understanding the ongoing state of work. This includes summaries of the work completed, which can be referred to as pre-compaction summaries or general summaries. A significant aspect of their content is the capture of "key state" information, particularly in relation to "summary compaction."

Beyond summarization, Session Notes also function as active state reminders, with "Paper v23.1" being cited as an example. Functionally, they serve as a "flush trigger" for context loading. An example of specific content that might be found within Session Notes is the detailing of the finalization of the NCD-CIE-LLM paper and its associated experiments, as recorded during a session on 2026-02-18.&lt;SEP&gt;Detailed records of work sessions, including summaries and active state reminders.&lt;SEP&gt;Detailed records of work sessions, including summaries and active state reminders.&lt;SEP&gt;Detailed records of work sessions, including summaries and active state reminders.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54584911fe0f3952d96167d568620e03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf138f605cebd36b4d1e832a3e1e39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77776675f0bb363ecfbbe31fb0e4cafa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-740c826e0488c9c7d4bb49a2bc4b77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77fb2e17e5b4e8bf73efceb26909e50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fa312b3a613954493f7372dd7f8b89e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ef545088384ee9d14b145ae009a44f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772910854</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Paper V23.1">
  <data key="d0">Paper V23.1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Paper V23.1 refers to a specific version of a document, research paper, or project. This entity is consistently designated and listed as an "Active State Reminder" within various session notes, indicating a particular status for the project or document. It is explicitly mentioned as an "Active State Reminder" within the 2026-02-17 Session Notes.

As a research paper project, Paper V23.1 underwent revisions based on feedback received from internal reviewers. Following these revisions, the paper was deemed ready for resubmission. It was subsequently submitted to CMT, a common system for managing submissions. Its recurrent mention in session notes highlights its significance as part of extensive work covered during these sessions.&lt;SEP&gt;Paper v23.1 is the specific document that was submitted to CMT.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific document or project version mentioned in session notes.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific document or project version mentioned in session notes.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific document or project version mentioned in session notes.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific document or project version mentioned in session notes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54584911fe0f3952d96167d568620e03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48404c33a0cecaca96752c576cc8ff1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e7140b8f3f101761721f48a25fbbb7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fa312b3a613954493f7372dd7f8b89e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0f4f4c5b62eaf87275657bec065d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ef545088384ee9d14b145ae009a44f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58b7644953ef75c0975b2aed17b0672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de95c6e776434a30a3b960742fb47652&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b7c6e043add1924b22fb12f4a845bad</data>
