<node id="Flush Trigger">
  <data key="d0">Flush Trigger</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mechanism or event that initiates the saving or processing of accumulated context, as described in the session notes.&lt;SEP&gt;Flush Trigger describes the purpose of a session, indicating it was for flushing rather than new work.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanism or event signifying that no new work was done in a session beyond context loading, initiating summary compaction.&lt;SEP&gt;An event or mechanism that marked the end or specific state of a session.&lt;SEP&gt;The purpose or function of the session described in the action item.&lt;SEP&gt;A mechanism or event that the session functioned as.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54584911fe0f3952d96167d568620e03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf138f605cebd36b4d1e832a3e1e39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-740c826e0488c9c7d4bb49a2bc4b77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9697e2fcc47861d37b8694c27fdf6af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13a57093e8a7a8c853ba4637e1a4e354&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8d5a8a323bc9df3696d4d06bbc6d8f6</data>
