<node id="Context Loading">
  <data key="d0">Context Loading</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Context Loading is identified as a process, activity, or operation that takes place during a session. Its core function involves the retrieval and preparation of relevant contextual information for that session, encompassing the loading of necessary context.

A defining characteristic of Context Loading is that no new work was performed beyond its execution within the session; it marked the extent of the work completed. Additionally, this process serves as a condition for a flush trigger. Its occurrence and details are typically documented and mentioned within the session notes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54584911fe0f3952d96167d568620e03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf138f605cebd36b4d1e832a3e1e39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-740c826e0488c9c7d4bb49a2bc4b77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9697e2fcc47861d37b8694c27fdf6af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-564d8cbe6d4c74180f4e5a59066a30ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acebf29512b1f172151cb83a3d9c8d0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13a57093e8a7a8c853ba4637e1a4e354&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8d5a8a323bc9df3696d4d06bbc6d8f6</data>
