<node id="Unknown">
  <data key="d0">Unknown</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e064beaa9addbc9ee14f687e59311381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad0e1255b938172ca134381d029ccfab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd0ccd8a9f7a8658474ff41f4568f053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38e9b054f469e1e12699cc361780a27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f8a20b859668d076e2131327e584f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c58b42bcfbdc99ab572d190b27de5882&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad9fb1e5163e6414596ae7be5069a0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b532fc0a0b97056a26a986eb3b68e8db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e5327a335f8e6829fb7146bfa56b6e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec8ad3036b56d46fd8e90ca2c3df9733&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fddb2cc14c43a22c2bff400f2e91900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21505e93a0cc67d7c52842393c4061dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2bfbe87d5ce5fcc4ebe045a23d0c8bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2948e4d867e4934b354be8aaec232e61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6eb4f09fefa949d587a5e642781696d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c133512663877544ce76399dec1202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a7d70bcf4d9abe91d1e8857f535f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acfca51e677015e2359e2c533733b33d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c69dd3d5ad9abafd29bc0eb1900f0d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c81a1607b189e4dccda6f296a585133&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eeb270a0d9ae6f5206f0a1aa6b2629f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-657295e8da90ebcecc66d3991617b8b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eee2c189ccaf551625d822442371f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-553970a05990c86011314bb088dd2739&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bdeda52180347e871c154fa8a5e6f40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-805fa7e9a6e788653ad117ed0227d7c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e527b91e6a9ad23487f23991185d3899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d400d5869eed285feebf30f08b829840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79ddda34c68c03295de8a44d1f990f6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0e25ce8b34a0336b469e6f8e4f36694&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebb4347b4c265fb1a8a24b5ff8611dbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32b91efbe6e5718dfa15ab0b00ab7fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a667a400dc093dec5aeac02a341e6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3ae3c1ef1d49f30b2e0d1d79ff7b93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f8980911843c949e318dafd147dd349&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72ba365e8bf622a7178a0ea539da5433&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f06ad9756d437f3ec57d576c17149e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33488833b7907af8855976c04d1a45b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ba301546b6ae101c68e73ce7078068&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68dd03cabc79b359a4f9a12e8628b7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dfa826c7c52d66bfc6ad79969fe0987&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-223207bb74fcb9e407f21062cc2e8466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baddfe598ce4b06af1660bd87bc93b51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-624f82c2f306963511da123121ec4085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b10fda63d615c42dfd5266faa4de97b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f1de4efc5e7b6ce50de1426a4a46cee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c676fbfb605498dc9758c93d6d6f28e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49a2a856b8bd05700b4f33eb914dd4e</data>
  <data key="d2">"Unknown" serves as a designation or status that signifies a lack of specified, identified, or designated information, particularly concerning identity, roles, or affiliations. It represents a state where definitive information regarding a particular attribute or responsibility has not been determined or communicated. This designation is consistently utilized across various contexts to denote an absence of explicit assignment or identification.

Specifically, "Unknown" is applied when the organizational affiliation or the role of a "Compaction Summary person" is not known or remains unspecified. It also functions as the status or designation for the owners of a decision when these individuals or groups are not identified or explicitly stated, thereby representing the unspecified proprietors of the decision.

In the context of task management and responsibility assignment, "Unknown" indicates that the person or entity designated as the owner of an action item has not been determined or communicated, or whose specific identity is not provided. This signifies an unassigned, unidentified, or unnamed individual or group responsible for the action item. "Unknown" is identified as the specified or designated owner for numerous action items, including V11, 129, "Complete Vault Overhaul Backlinking", Action Item 142, Action Item 121, Action Item 122, Action Item 127, Action Item 119, "Resubmit Paper v23.1 to CMT", Action Item 2026-02-17, and the NCD-CIE Open Dataset Search action item, consistently representing the unspecified individual or role responsible when a specific individual or group has not been identified.&lt;SEP&gt;The individual designated as the owner of the action item, whose name is not provided.&lt;SEP&gt;The stated owner of the action item, which is currently unspecified.&lt;SEP&gt;The specified value for the owner property of Action Item 163, indicating no specific individual is assigned.&lt;SEP&gt;A placeholder value indicating that a specific detail, such as an owner, is not specified.&lt;SEP&gt;Unknown is the designated owner for this particular action item.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772911335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skills Installed">
  <data key="d0">Skills Installed</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Skills Installed is a person entity meticulously documented and referenced within an Obsidian knowledge graph. This entity was created on 2026-02-17, with associated knowledge graph and interaction data established on the same date.

While explicitly identified as a person within the knowledge graph, the specific role and organization of Skills Installed are currently unknown. The entity's activities and interactions are comprehensively logged, including details about paper revisions, skill installations, and project work. Daily interactions involving Skills Installed are also tracked and recorded within Obsidian daily notes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-33c82f85cdf1f3f6b459569c71f52f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ada2e9500cf083516501a8b590959545&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de7d2b034444ef30c5cd263afdaf88fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcffafc2471db66eeb67f5125adb0c07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-521f31ad3498d511d1daef16699339a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77fb2e17e5b4e8bf73efceb26909e50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4e9e850cc678da23e40adf85f868cd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f9a385ebc3487ab67289add07185a9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772593458</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ClawHub">
  <data key="d0">ClawHub</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">ClawHub is a comprehensive platform, system, service, or ecosystem that serves as a central source and primary repository for installing various software skills. It provides these capabilities, enabling users to obtain and integrate diverse functionalities into their systems.

The platform is intrinsically linked with the ClawHub Command Line Interface (CLI). This CLI is the primary tool utilized to facilitate the process of adding or installing skills directly from ClawHub. Furthermore, ClawHub functions as the source from which the ClawHub CLI itself is installed, establishing it as a complete ecosystem for managing both the interface and the skills it deploys.

Operationally, ClawHub implements and is responsible for rate limits. These rate limits have previously necessitated decisions to increase the delay between skill installations, likely to manage system load or resource allocation. The platform is also subject to regular monitoring; it is checked weekly, often by a cron job, to identify and integrate new skills and updates into its offerings.&lt;SEP&gt;A platform or service that imposes rate limits on skill installations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-33c82f85cdf1f3f6b459569c71f52f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ad29c3ef4ea9d4073b8f21e15af929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b066b3b635168888a671932f0d4aa9c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22b397f0555571eb32ef1aaf94d5749&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-129d795f9b647690a68ead0a15b17c08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a690dc7d0a9c006978732d3edc11a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a9809eefacfad853cbe9eca4de35242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e66410fb2c2fa832a2c0adcd41f9368&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563e9b5c607a87d47046fea356d51100&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19dd0bede6e30ba44b3f5793a1e6a99e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8810b0cc19fdc55c82c76db548698a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f681751f508fd167c31bbe1d202056b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1d361334741e195fd3cc01498c5d61d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-280669fa49c70eb7ad44fa8711ecb2d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9e9ea9f9ef3e6e49b68f230ad0b56ef</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772610150</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ClawHub CLI">
  <data key="d0">ClawHub CLI</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ClawHub CLI is a command-line interface (CLI) tool developed for interaction with the ClawHub system. Its core purpose is to facilitate the addition, installation, and management of skills within this ecosystem.

The ClawHub CLI tool is installed via npm. Specifically, it is installed globally using the command `npm install -g clawhub`, ensuring it is an accessible component for skill management as part of the broader ClawHub system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-33c82f85cdf1f3f6b459569c71f52f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ad29c3ef4ea9d4073b8f21e15af929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b066b3b635168888a671932f0d4aa9c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22b397f0555571eb32ef1aaf94d5749&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-129d795f9b647690a68ead0a15b17c08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3b0e643ebc37d6e483ed820982ca193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a690dc7d0a9c006978732d3edc11a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a9809eefacfad853cbe9eca4de35242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cba83ad815daf324fb66f8121ca897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e66410fb2c2fa832a2c0adcd41f9368&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563e9b5c607a87d47046fea356d51100&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f681751f508fd167c31bbe1d202056b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772824634</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Npm">
  <data key="d0">Npm</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Npm is a prominent package manager, specifically identified as the Node.js package manager. It serves the crucial function of installing various software packages and tools. Examples of its utility include the installation of command-line interfaces such as the ClawHub CLI, as well as other software like OpenClaw. Notably, Npm is an integral component, bundled with Node.js 22 within the upgraded Docker image.&lt;SEP&gt;A package manager used to install ClawHub CLI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-33c82f85cdf1f3f6b459569c71f52f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3ad29c3ef4ea9d4073b8f21e15af929&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b066b3b635168888a671932f0d4aa9c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22b397f0555571eb32ef1aaf94d5749&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be1a879a09130cca84364cf74d7544cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e66410fb2c2fa832a2c0adcd41f9368&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563e9b5c607a87d47046fea356d51100&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-000e5cbc3c5b62de4af4981edce03d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f681751f508fd167c31bbe1d202056b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772609285</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Google Drive">
  <data key="d0">Google Drive</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Google Drive is a comprehensive cloud storage and file synchronization service provided by Google, functioning as a central repository for uploading, storing, hosting, and sharing a wide array of digital files and documents. As a cloud-based storage and collaboration platform, it integrates with automation systems to facilitate the management of different file versions and revisions, which are uploaded and organized according to defined conventions. The platform is also utilized for organizing and saving paper files, acting as a crucial designated hub for file management and collaboration across various applications.

The service is extensively utilized in academic, research, professional, and educational contexts. Academically, it supports the upload of specific versions of English manuscripts, Thai translation files, completed Thai documents, and final academic papers, including their PDF and LaTeX versions, notably those related to the v23.1 Revision, and specific paper revisions like v7 and v8. It hosts file types such as PDFs and .tex files, including the RAG Second Brain Paper (V15), PDF Final 12pg, and the research paper "Multi-Graph &amp; Ontology for AI." For educational content, Google Drive stores materials like the "DevOps with VibeCoding" course content, finished course materials, course documents, and slides.

Beyond academia, Google Drive serves as a critical service for various team-related documentation, encompassing team guides such as the Academic Paper Team Guide, completed guides, and professionally formatted Team Manuals (including versions V3 and V4) along with at least five associated professional DOCX guides. It is the designated platform for uploading final books produced by writing teams, including complete books generated in Full Auto Mode, storing them in DOCX format, and serving as the destination for the final delivered book. Furthermore, Google Drive accommodates enterprise reports like generated reports, the ClawdBot Enterprise Deployment Report, the Daily Cost Report, the HA_30_Complex_Dashboards.docx file, the 30 Complex Dashboards Report (v1), and other dashboard report documents. Diverse other files, including deliverables, generated documents, AI News Digests (e.g., AI News Digest 2026-02-22), translated Thai versions of documents, trip planning documents, English and Thai versions of novels, and general paper versions, are uploaded, stored, viewed, and organized on the platform.&lt;SEP&gt;A cloud storage service used for uploading and storing documents, including versions of revised papers and project reports.&lt;SEP&gt;A cloud storage service used for hosting the HA_30_Complex_Dashboards.docx document.&lt;SEP&gt;A cloud storage service where the HA_30_Complex_Dashboards.docx document is stored.&lt;SEP&gt;Google Drive is a cloud storage service where paper files are stored according to a naming convention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-33c82f85cdf1f3f6b459569c71f52f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-747382645d4ed066b3e5ef8307a73acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-771986aa17685fe6999e419c1c67ae69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65dccfd3aa8c2845e69d1620ba57b3ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8071a02051a6907a1d6bcf1d18784337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98ee600c3aaf8c0514fc103e242dc4e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cb2da7ce21279bc4524ae53da55f5f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a148d70205b447fa0880b01f6090cb4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f149b5b7744bf9b94dd99c2730c6f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a5a2a5ee9379f99260bf82e77d61e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b7ba42f6f46d6daa16d9a38d06454da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca39d930338f6b1274506ff5a5005957&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eaa520657989ec2fc6405a732d52292&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf138f605cebd36b4d1e832a3e1e39b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2239c6d05ef20d0c2099bfe102d8578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a86793a1f22c5b47b2656851af199c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a9809eefacfad853cbe9eca4de35242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-118f2c92999f532d1ba41c8ebba99b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-351c38e6239e7aefbeccda46e10b207e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c371260389e0782fbfb49af2d151de86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da16976f6a8b1abecf041605a040a8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f4d700c803a895f4d5c3b79bf2a8218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac42e4b444b2aa35a9817c58b1eaadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60b689f3d71dd57c707b347058466c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29838b6eb58a146f57cc1b18e2349ce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6287da837abc320ea063bf0536adfe6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a5b9736ebbe3190b02500066610a61e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de95c6e776434a30a3b960742fb47652&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be32808c942011a178df2564dffe6d3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8268912354c6ad40989f1deca0c0990f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181b4f905977b5bffcec8667be7beb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abf907c5e36499f7a4ccbff7a18a5031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46acd3e509aa2a1265a39d2c0a5e6f5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-962708e2b38cf807f5da24a5a99fe6a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734ec6fc710d1be198572ead525f9006&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7540722cdec2c35b0cf85a5979b43057&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16aa16294c1a8087f5e8fa6f3e8f6bc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465cfc7fed7647f14ac063c527100a11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c2753f45f158b0a6204d83e9fa7880a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e446842d3412fd960