<node id="Paper Revisions">
  <data key="d0">Paper Revisions</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Paper Revisions refers to a comprehensive and iterative process focused on making changes, updates, and improvements to a paper. This activity is considered an ongoing project and a general category of work, particularly prevalent within the context of academic papers. The primary objective of these revisions is to refine the paper's content and structure, specifically to address and integrate reviewer feedback and concerns.

This process involves a series of updates and corrections, which are systematically documented. These changes are typically recorded in a daily log, often appearing as a dedicated section within it, detailing the progress. The outcomes of these revision efforts are new versions of the paper. Notably, versions v7 and v8 are frequently cited as specific examples or stages within this project, having been completed to address particular issues such as differentiability, compute feasibility, and Knowledge Graph (KG) snapshot dates, in addition to resolving general reviewer concerns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-33c82f85cdf1f3f6b459569c71f52f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65dccfd3aa8c2845e69d1620ba57b3ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8071a02051a6907a1d6bcf1d18784337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a5a2a5ee9379f99260bf82e77d61e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b7ba42f6f46d6daa16d9a38d06454da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a9809eefacfad853cbe9eca4de35242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-118f2c92999f532d1ba41c8ebba99b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-351c38e6239e7aefbeccda46e10b207e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da16976f6a8b1abecf041605a040a8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f4d700c803a895f4d5c3b79bf2a8218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-101606dc1a1c38f13f50aac3f37c0d07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-572bc319ace0969403b23edbb05f1603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff7e5c1e27b82737e07d089640954be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc701838f07233735cb275776b21683</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772910415</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
