</node>
<node id="Google OAuth Credentials">
  <data key="d0">Google OAuth Credentials</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Google OAuth Credentials are a set of authorization data that belong to Anirach. These credentials are fundamentally utilized in the authorization code exchange process, an essential step during system setup. Specifically, they play a crucial role in the Google Calendar integration process. During this integration and setup, the Google OAuth Credentials are used to generate an authorization URI, a key component for initiating the authorization flow. This generation of the authorization URI is also associated with a step-by-step chat process, further facilitating the integration with Google Calendar.&lt;SEP&gt;Credentials belonging to Anirach, used for authorization during the Google Calendar integration setup.&lt;SEP&gt;Credentials used to generate the authorization URL during the Google Calendar integration process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-70c5932aa815cd6eef3ea2972206ea5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113056c9501e9b2d79be577e20d93410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1aac26b6f017550e6b8be634bc44e292&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0bb009da2afea369e4c821ce1e24395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b09e05a7e31f0c9576ad10f1a2885e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e55ed8097afa7059c8bb422a3149921a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d526320401eafeca2cd894cd415353dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-932186885558d1449f2179e933b5649a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bdd05384cd19411b8d7358f5ff4a53e</data>
