<node id="Multi-Source RAG Framework">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Source RAG Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Multi-Source RAG Framework is a proposed research framework for Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG). It is comprehensively detailed in the "RAG Second Brain Paper."

This framework is designed to integrate a variety of retrieval methods to enhance its capabilities. Specifically, it combines dense vector retrieval, co-occurrence-based statistical retrieval (which utilizes PPMI - Pointwise Mutual Information), and knowledge graph traversal, further enhanced by OWL ontological reasoning. This multi-faceted approach aims to leverage different strengths in information retrieval for RAG applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fa0b04516491978cd7f2fd3497bd74a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbbf68c07d5785152cb568cb44c097d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7500ba1991c8bf7c275040fb5d136c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-319918c1dd29c15f300842daf00bc7e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d8f0cc2dda28211617dff6e3558df7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8cf8fc2d96758ea18301e0ea37632a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041d128ced8892285239ffadbdd877cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8268912354c6ad40989f1deca0c0990f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-565cbd3991fde971e7c72b941083b823</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772601500</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Batch">
  <data key="d0">Batch</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Batch refers to a discrete processing event or a group of interactions, frequently sourced from Memory, that typically occurs at a specific time. It functions as an automated process or interaction, indicating how data is processed or updated within a system.

Fundamentally, Batch serves as a method or system identified as the source for a decision, its associated context, and as the origin point for various action items. It is consistently described as the specified source type, the designated source, the origin, and the source method by which action items are generated, identified, entered, or classified. This includes being the designated source category, the source category from which an action item originated, or the source or method by which an action item was generated.

For instance, Batch is explicitly cited as the origin for Action Item 129, the specified source category for Action Item 126, the designated source classification for Action Item 121, the source method for Action Item 122, a specified source for Action Item 119, and the designated source method for Action Item 161. It also represents the origin or mechanism by which action items, such as Action Item 127, are generated or added, functioning as the source system or process from which they originated. Additionally, it is identified as the source for 'Rebuild Week 6 Sub-Agent (PPTX)'. More broadly, Batch signifies a method or origin for the creation or processing of items and acts as a context or entity involved in a research paper proposing a multi-agent RAG system.&lt;SEP&gt;Batch is the source or origin method for the action item.&lt;SEP&gt;The designated source or origin from which the action item was generated.&lt;SEP&gt;The source or method by which the action item was generated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2f30a8d91993f68af9395b1e286ae615&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f197e592637ef1737a9a8857200343b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f8a20b859668d076e2131327e584f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-565cbd3991fde971e7c72b941083b823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b532fc0a0b97056a26a986eb3b68e8db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fddb2cc14c43a22c2bff400f2e91900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21505e93a0cc67d7c52842393c4061dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03acda338173ae2441ba9aa9f0a604ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-454306d201a2fb212f19fe3fa3ddc91f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c69dd3d5ad9abafd29bc0eb1900f0d20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba754fb7a934f88d986d68a77c5aedf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97eee2c189ccaf551625d822442371f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-553970a05990c86011314bb088dd2739&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bdeda52180347e871c154fa8a5e6f40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-805fa7e9a6e788653ad117ed0227d7c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acebf29512b1f172151cb83a3d9c8d0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d400d5869eed285feebf30f08b829840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14eec4ba21399e018e3f0aacefcb6f3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0e25ce8b34a0336b469e6f8e4f36694&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e27a41e07f2a1a24017c7da0aad718b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a667a400dc093dec5aeac02a341e6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f06ad9756d437f3ec57d576c17149e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a49ce3e3a6ea95d15d086aa1c70e6dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62ea5e131e305f309112c1dee0c52336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bec3af3bde15c1b64211df6fa35c0ab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90d78c13443367a6638fb67e23cf0558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b1d23c22473007c4333aa91e8f8d366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-624f82c2f306963511da123121ec4085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b10fda63d615c42dfd5266faa4de97b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813c4f52fd587bfecf3d1d07dba8dea0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4dc7b3055f1c86726d780fc180a8345&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c676fbfb605498dc9758c93d6d6f28e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a49a2a856b8bd05700b4f33eb914dd4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04e12e42246ce3393cda4585cac03ce1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0675b88b9f4cf07a0e2ae3b73847404d</data>
