<node id="MEMORY.md">
  <data key="d0">MEMORY.md</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">MEMORY.md is a specific markdown file that functions as a central repository or master memory file, designed to maintain comprehensive project information. This document is consistently updated with various details, including specific project references like ChartSense AI, a full list of installed skills, records of important events or event summaries, and a new review date.

The file is designed to be updated with extracted key learnings, crucial decisions, significant facts, and new lessons derived from session transcripts and the Auto-Reflection process. Updates to MEMORY.md are consistently performed during a process known as "Memory Maintenance," which is often facilitated and reviewed by a `memory-maintenance` cron job, ensuring it contains current and relevant information. Additionally, it requires an update after Coding Manual v3 is completed.

Historically, MEMORY.md was involved in a data duplication issue, where identified redundancies were removed as part of a process termed "3.1KB Duplication Removal." Due to its critical function, deleting MEMORY.md is now considered a dangerous action and requires explicit confirmation.&lt;SEP&gt;A memory file that was updated with project details, installed skills list, and important events.&lt;SEP&gt;A memory file that was updated with project details, installed skills list, and important events.&lt;SEP&gt;A memory file that was updated with project details, installed skills list, and important events.</data>
