<node id="Weekly Memory Maintenance">
  <data key="d0">Weekly Memory Maintenance</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Weekly Memory Maintenance is defined as a recurring, routine, and regularly scheduled activity or process. It is performed on a weekly basis, typically around 3 AM. The core function of this process involves the thorough review of memory files, followed by their subsequent update.

A key component of Weekly Memory Maintenance is the updating of the file designated as `MEMORY.md`. While it is a routine process, an example of its execution was noted on 2026-02-15. Some descriptions also suggest that this activity is performed by an entity referred to as "Memory Maintenance," implying a system or agent responsible for its consistent execution.&lt;SEP&gt;A regular activity involving reviewing memory files and updating MEMORY.md, performed on 2026-02-15.&lt;SEP&gt;A regular activity involving reviewing memory files and updating MEMORY.md, performed on 2026-02-15.&lt;SEP&gt;A regular activity involving reviewing memory files and updating MEMORY.md, performed on 2026-02-15.&lt;SEP&gt;A regular activity involving reviewing memory files and updating MEMORY.md, performed on 2026-02-15.</data>
