  <data key="d0">Prisma</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prisma is an ORM (Object-Relational Mapper) technology primarily utilized for backend development. It serves as a crucial component within the technology stack of several distinct projects and systems. Specifically, Prisma is employed in the development of the Personal Books Management System. It is also an integral tool used in the creation and ongoing development of the AI Research Dashboard. Furthermore, Prisma is recognized as part of the technology stack for the Bookshelf App project.&lt;SEP&gt;An ORM (Object-Relational Mapper) used as part of the technology stack for the Personal Books Management System.&lt;SEP&gt;A technology used for building new projects, specifically mentioned for an e-commerce dashboard.&lt;SEP&gt;An ORM used in the stack of the Personal Books Management System; version 5 was used due to breaking changes in version 7.&lt;SEP&gt;Prisma is an ORM (Object-Relational Mapper) used in building the AI Research Dashboard.</data>
