<node id="Systemd Service">
  <data key="d0">Systemd Service</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Systemd Service is a fundamental component within the Linux operating system, functioning as a method and daemon management mechanism for controlling system processes. It is integral to the Linux initialization system and service manager, Systemd.

A primary application of a Systemd Service is to configure specific applications or daemons for automatic execution upon system boot. For instance, a service unit named `lobsterboard.service` was created specifically for LobsterBoard. This ensures LobsterBoard can auto-start reliably when the system initializes, demonstrating how Systemd Service facilitates process management and guarantees the desired operational state of services.&lt;SEP&gt;A Systemd service is a background process configuration managed by the system, which was cleaned up during the migration.&lt;SEP&gt;A daemon management mechanism in Linux, specifically referring to `lobsterboard.service` created for auto-starting LobsterBoard.&lt;SEP&gt;A daemon management mechanism in Linux, specifically referring to `lobsterboard.service` created for auto-starting LobsterBoard.&lt;SEP&gt;A daemon management mechanism in Linux, specifically referring to `lobsterboard.service` created for auto-starting LobsterBoard.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-698aa50ab28f0e3566cb6e574a6621f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77fb2e17e5b4e8bf73efceb26909e50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ed29f1c61ff580597801b78ee3bb1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cba83ad815daf324fb66f8121ca897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2137ff35cca3b6a1f530734272b671a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c6144f7eea8f9ff2209417a52185401&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffed2e0d5a98ce8d9cb5106e19cdcce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f87202506d912406b3336864391a105</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772824623</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAG Second Brain Paper V15">
  <data key="d0">RAG Second Brain Paper V15</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">RAG Second Brain Paper v15 is a document detailing final results, including performance metrics and statistical significance, related to learned gating.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG Second Brain Paper V15 is a paper detailing final results and page reduction, created on 2026-02-16, and is related to knowledge graphs.&lt;SEP&gt;A paper that is a project type, detailing final results and page reduction details, created on 2026-02-16 within Obsidian.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG Second Brain Paper V15 is a project described as a paper containing final results and page reduction details.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG Second Brain Paper v15 is a project document that includes final results and page reduction details, presenting metrics like Sigmoid R@10 and Softmax R@10.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG Second Brain Paper V15 is a specific version of a paper that achieved final results using Learned Gating.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-698aa50ab28f0e3566cb6e574a6621f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09ddcd570d6b2e7e45dfe04d63a2b1dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4f719cbd2b4a06b6e395856df09e63b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18d26eb346378dcde8c223fffaf61172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f174664d1cea2b5dff02b5d7d0e6a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6c15de56039236682f9856e47cab92d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772609668</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sigmoid R@10">
  <data key="d0">Sigmoid R@10</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Sigmoid R@10 is a performance metric, specifically a Recall@10 (R@10) value, that utilizes a Sigmoid activation function. It achieved a reported value of 0.923.

This metric was obtained through the application of Learned Gating, a method used to achieve its performance. Sigmoid R@10 demonstrates significant efficacy, showing an 18.4% improvement over the RRF Baseline (or RRF). This achievement is notably documented in the RAG Second Brain Paper v15.&lt;SEP&gt;A performance metric result of 0.923 for "Learned Gating", showing an 18.4% improvement over the "RRF Baseline".&lt;SEP&gt;Sigmoid R@10 is a specific performance metric, achieving 0.923 (0.889, 0.950), which is 18.4% over RRF.&lt;SEP&gt;Sigmoid R@10 is a performance metric with a result of 0.923, showing an 18.4% improvement over RRF Baseline.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific metric or result of 0.923 achieved using Learned Gating in the RAG Second Brain Paper v15.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific R@10 score (0.923) achieved with Learned Gating using a Sigmoid function in the RAG Second Brain Paper.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-698aa50ab28f0e3566cb6e574a6621f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4b9540765c9116547992f4b4a476e1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d113e8b1edad4ebb129a2a094a883e18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31d3997afc563a8575185bcc2410347a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a5a2a5ee9379f99260bf82e77d61e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02fed1956b021d157c9aefe4e22c23a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ea6d7871cd452fe1d5c6536cbd0937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2dd1bf46bef690dc3e5e67e19c9b119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f174664d1cea2b5dff02b5d7d0e6a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6c15de56039236682f9856e47cab92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff7e5c1e27b82737e07d089640954be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc701838f07233735cb275776b21683</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772910419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Softmax R@10">
  <data key="d0">Softmax R@10</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Softmax R@10 is a performance metric, specifically identified as a Recall@10 (R@10) value, that utilizes a Softmax activation function. This metric is reported with a consistent value of 0.911.

It is considered a final result metric, with this particular value having been achieved through the application of Learned Gating. The context for this performance metric and its reported value is documented in the RAG Second Brain Paper v15.&lt;SEP&gt;A performance metric result of 0.911 for "Learned Gating".&lt;SEP&gt;Softmax R@10 is a specific performance metric, achieving 0.911 (0.874, 0.939).&lt;SEP&gt;Softmax R@10 is a performance metric with a result of 0.911.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific metric or result of 0.911 achieved using Learned Gating in the RAG Second Brain Paper v15.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific R@10 score (0.911) achieved with Learned Gating using a Softmax function in the RAG Second Brain Paper.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-698aa50ab28f0e3566cb6e574a6621f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4b9540765c9116547992f4b4a476e1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d113e8b1edad4ebb129a2a094a883e18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31d3997afc563a8575185bcc2410347a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a5a2a5ee9379f99260bf82e77d61e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02fed1956b021d157c9aefe4e22c23a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ea6d7871cd452fe1d5c6536cbd0937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2dd1bf46bef690dc3e5e67e19c9b119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f174664d1cea2b5dff02b5d7d0e6a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6c15de56039236682f9856e47cab92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff7e5c1e27b82737e07d089640954be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc701838f07233735cb275776b21683</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772910419</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RRF Baseline">
  <data key="d0">RRF Baseline</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RRF Baseline is a performance metric that functions as a baseline method for comparative analysis. It specifically represents a Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) approach.

This baseline metric holds a reported value of 0.779, which is further specified as R@10 (Reciprocal Rank at 10). Its primary purpose is to serve as a benchmark against which other results are evaluated, particularly for comparison with outcomes derived from Learned Gating.

The RRF Baseline, along with its reported value and application in comparative studies, is extensively utilized and documented in the RAG Second Brain Paper v15.&lt;SEP&gt;A baseline performance metric of 0.779 used for comparison in the "RAG Second Brain Paper v15".&lt;SEP&gt;RRF Baseline is a reference performance metric, with a value of 0.779 (0.730, 0.823).&lt;SEP&gt;RRF Baseline is a performance metric used for comparison, with a result of 0.779.&lt;SEP&gt;A baseline metric or result of 0.779 used for comparison in the RAG Second Brain Paper v15.&lt;SEP&gt;A baseline (0.779 R@10) used for comparison against the Learned Gating results in the RAG Second Brain Paper.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-698aa50ab28f0e3566cb6e574a6621f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4b9540765c9116547992f4b4a476e1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d113e8b1edad4ebb129a2a094a883e18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31d3997afc563a8575185bcc2410347a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a5a2a5ee9379f99260bf82e77d61e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02fed1956b021d157c9aefe4e22c23a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ea6d7871cd452fe1d5c6536cbd0937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2dd1bf46bef690dc3e5e67e19c9b119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f174664d1cea2b5dff02b5d7d0e6a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6c15de56039236682f9856e47cab92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff7e5c1e27b82737e07d089640954be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc701838f07233735cb275776b21683</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772910411</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statistical Significance">
  <data key="d0">Statistical Significance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Statistical Significance is a fundamental statistical concept and measure that assesses the reliability of observed results. It quantifies the probability that a result or relationship has occurred not by random chance, or, conversely, the probability that it *is* due to chance. This reliability is typically indicated by a p-value.

For the RAG Second Brain Paper v15, Statistical Significance is reported as a key finding for its final results. Within this context, a p-value of less than 0.001 (p &lt; 0.001) is consistently noted, sometimes specified as a bootstrap p-value. This indicates that the observed results are highly significant and are very unlikely to be attributable to mere chance.&lt;SEP&gt;A statistical measure indicating the reliability of the observed results, reported as p &lt; 0.001.&lt;SEP&gt;Statistical Significance is a measure of the reliability of the observed results, indicated by p &lt; 0.001.&lt;SEP&gt;Statistical Significance is a measure indicating that the observed results are unlikely due to chance, with p &lt; 0.001.&lt;SEP&gt;A statistical property indicating that results, such as those in the RAG Second Brain Paper v15, are unlikely to have occurred by chance, specifically noted as p &lt; 0.001.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure (p &lt; 0.001, bootstrap) indicating the reliability of the observed performance differences in the RAG Second Brain Paper.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-698aa50ab28f0e3566cb6e574a6621f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4b9540765c9116547992f4b4a476e1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d113e8b1edad4ebb129a2a094a883e18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31d3997afc563a8575185bcc2410347a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a5a2a5ee9379f99260bf82e77d61e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02fed1956b021d157c9aefe4e22c23a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ea6d7871cd452fe1d5c6536cbd0937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2dd1bf46bef690dc3e5e67e19c9b119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f174664d1cea2b5dff02b5d7d0e6a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6c15de56039236682f9856e47cab92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff7e5c1e27b82737e07d089640954be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc701838f07233735cb275776b21683</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772910417</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Learned Gating">
  <data key="d0">Learned Gating</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Learned Gating is predominantly understood as a method, concept, or technique, consistently associated with the "RAG Second Brain Paper v15." It is described as a specific multi-source fusion method implemented within the project detailed in this paper, which has a dedicated training task and is slated for training.

Within the context of the "RAG Second Brain Paper v15," Learned Gating serves to produce or achieve the final research and experimental results, demonstrating significant performance improvements. Its performance is quantified by specific metrics, including Sigmoid R@10 and Softmax R@10 scores. Notably, a Sigmoid R@10 value of 0.923 has been reported for this method.

While the overwhelming majority of descriptions firmly establish Learned Gating as a technical approach or system, one source also identifies it as a person associated with final research results. However, this interpretation contradicts the detailed technical context, implementation specifics, and quantifiable performance metrics consistently attributed to Learned Gating as a method throughout the various descriptions. Therefore, it is primarily recognized and detailed as a methodological component within the research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-698aa50ab28f0e3566cb6e574a6621f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4b9540765c9116547992f4b4a476e1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d113e8b1edad4ebb129a2a094a883e18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31d3997afc563a8575185bcc2410347a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a5a2a5ee9379f99260bf82e77d61e46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02fed1956b021d157c9aefe4e22c23a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-defbb01c471de1f9b119c0fb594cfce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03ea6d7871cd452fe1d5c6536cbd0937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2dd1bf46bef690dc3e5e67e19c9b119&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f174664d1cea2b5dff02b5d7d0e6a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e788ba3e64d85e6086e324e92e602039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a2f4932683deada51cf0bb651a5811&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6c15de56039236682f9856e47cab92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ff7e5c1e27b82737e07d089640954be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc701838f07233735cb275776b21683</data>
