</node>
<node id="Bookshelf App">
  <data key="d0">Bookshelf App</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bookshelf App is a software application project developed by Anirach Mingkhwan. It is currently an in-progress project, prominently listed within the Knowledge Graph's project index.

This application is built using a contemporary technology stack. Its development leverages Next.js, specifically Next.js 14, alongside shadcn/ui for the user interface, and Prisma, with Prisma 5, for data management. While the project has a noted relationship with PostgreSQL, its core database technology for the current build is SQLite. The Bookshelf App is designed to incorporate essential data models including Book, Author, and Genre.&lt;SEP&gt;Bookshelf App is a project developed at King Mongkut's University of Technology North Bangkok.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-838a7372037dd9d7583be5b6dfb14047&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e3f7a26a4c8d639a7927de46537f385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-558b6d2c1acd0ead39cb816a545fc170&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5156974771cb937584c35af037182dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-324bd841922db4db30ba10360e372195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a000ee9fe32af97bf41c1cb4481251e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd5511d906f079895d9f4230f3c92969&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4d74588847aeaab263c27d6a5d7245f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28873878f8dcbd5abb8ed630f432e8af</data>
