<node id="Agent Teams">
  <data key="d0">Agent Teams</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">"Agent Teams" refers to two distinct concepts identified in the provided descriptions.

Firstly, Agent Teams are understood as groups of agents or functionalities that are driven by Artificial Intelligence within the described work. These teams primarily provide support for various stages of course development, including tasks such as course preparation, curriculum design, and assessment creation, particularly within the context of Education Technology. A defining characteristic of these Agent Teams is their utilization of an Obsidian vault, which functions as their shared knowledge base.

Secondly, "Agent Teams" is also identified as a specific entity within a knowledge graph. In this particular context, it is classified as a person and is related to knowledge graphs. However, the specific role and organizational affiliation of this "Agent Teams" entity are currently unknown.&lt;SEP&gt;Agent teams are entities that support various educational processes like course preparation, curriculum design, and assessment creation.&lt;SEP&gt;All teams mandated to follow the Google Drive File Convention for their file uploads.&lt;SEP&gt;Agent Teams are entities that use Obsidian as a workbook for various projects and activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The groups of agents for whom the Obsidian vault serves as a shared knowledge base.&lt;SEP&gt;The groups of agents for whom the Obsidian vault serves as a shared knowledge base.&lt;SEP&gt;The groups of agents for whom the Obsidian vault serves as a shared knowledge base.</data>
