<node id="Markdown">
  <data key="d0">Markdown</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Markdown is a lightweight markup language primarily used for formatting plain text documents. It functions as a versatile tool across various domains, often facilitating efficient data organization and conversion processes.

In the realm of knowledge management, Markdown serves as a fundamental basis, particularly within applications like Obsidian, where it is widely supported for creating and structuring content. Beyond general plain text formatting, it is also utilized extensively in document production workflows.

Markdown can act as an input format for book content, frequently undergoing conversion to DOCX. It also serves as an intermediate file format during the broader book production process. Its capabilities extend to format conversion generally, including its application in creating professional PDFs, and it is listed as a file format option for specific outputs, such as the Thai Translation Output.&lt;SEP&gt;A language used for content creation and knowledge management within Obsidian.&lt;SEP&gt;A language used for content creation and knowledge management within Obsidian.&lt;SEP&gt;A language used for content creation and knowledge management within Obsidian.</data>
