<node id="System Optimization">
  <data key="d0">System Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">System Optimization can refer to two distinct concepts based on the provided descriptions.

Firstly, System Optimization is identified as a process of performance tuning. This process is focused on improving overall system performance and explicitly included specific fixes, such as those related to memory search. It is described as an activity that was applied or undertaken to achieve these performance improvements.

Secondly, System Optimization is also described as a named entity, specifically a person. This individual is involved in conducting performance tuning sessions and is associated with applying various fixes during these sessions.</data>
