<node id="Memory Files">
  <data key="d0">Memory Files</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Memory Files refer to a specific category of digital files and documents containing memory data or information. These files are consistently identified as originating from the period of February 12-14. Their primary purpose is to be reviewed during the Memory Maintenance process, which is sometimes described as a weekly activity. This process involves the examination of the digital information from these particular dates as part of ongoing memory maintenance procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Files containing records of past activities and information that are reviewed and processed by agents.&lt;SEP&gt;Memory Files are data files that are reviewed by the Auto-Reflection Process and used by the Session Memory Miner Process.</data>
