  <data key="d0">ACM</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">ACM is an organization. It is consistently described as an entry listed within an index, specifically referred to as the "Organizations Index" or "Organizations index". This listing indicates ACM's presence within the broader context of a knowledge graph, with some descriptions further specifying it as being within the 'Organizations' index of the Obsidian knowledge graph.&lt;SEP&gt;ACM is a professional organization for computing, also serving as a target journal for academic papers.&lt;SEP&gt;A resource or database used by the Literature-Search skill.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific top-tier journal or publisher that sets publication standards.&lt;SEP&gt;An organization and a source for academic search.</data>
