<node id="Course Team">
  <data key="d0">Course Team</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Course Team is identified as a collective entity, typically referred to as one of five specific teams of agents operating within a larger project, or as an implied functional area. This team is primarily focused on developing courses and creating educational content, specifically managing materials such as slides and textbooks for various courses. The Course Team is also associated with knowledge graphs.

Structurally, the Course Team is described as being composed of 10 agents and supported by a dedicated professional guide. The team is further noted for its responsibility in creating and managing the Vibe Coding Antigravity project. Additionally, the Course Team was mentioned in a work log, reporting no active sessions on February 21st, 2026.&lt;SEP&gt;A team with 7 agents.&lt;SEP&gt;Course Team is one of the five agent teams, consisting of 7 agents for course development.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the agent teams that received new agents (`Video-Script-Writer Agent`, `Lab-Designer Agent`, `Accessibility-Checker Agent`) during the Major Agent Team Upgrade.&lt;SEP&gt;A team that received 8 new skills.&lt;SEP&gt;The Course Team is an agent team consisting of 7 agents: course-architect, curriculum-designer, content-writer, slide-designer, assessment-creator, book-compiler, and course-reviewer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d395d729f7f4af176337bfefc3a79dd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e50f018ab794854428e9bfc66b36eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c2753f45f158b0a6204d83e9fa7880a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-570c1687de41e99a692ad24992a2accd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6b7611801b56d161d9e4809cd690f58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f18c72310dfe68bd9a70bc2f54ec35b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed7db0d09c2f6c23c342cd0451173c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b394110aeea60586b9d87bbb1349ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-572bc319ace0969403b23edbb05f1603&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a2f4932683deada51cf0bb651a5811&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6c15de56039236682f9856e47cab92d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61736ce38c27461a2b10ba4645d7dc0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37056b34934d569bff0b96c6e8991103</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772609969</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UX/UI Designer Agent">
  <data key="d0">UX/UI Designer Agent</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The UX/UI Designer Agent is an intelligent software agent that operates based on the Opus Model. It is specifically designed to be integrated into a Coding Team, where its primary focus is on various critical aspects of user experience and user interface design.

This agent's specialization encompasses interface design, ensuring visual polish, enhancing overall usability, and implementing responsive design principles across projects. It utilizes expertise in specific front-end technologies, including Shadcn/UI and Tailwind CSS. A fundamental aspect of its operation is its strict adherence to Anti-AI-Slop Design Principles, aiming to produce high-quality, non-generic designs.

The UX/UI Designer Agent is typically deployed for a range of design-centric tasks. These include executing UI polish, developing new screens, conducting comprehensive UX reviews, and contributing to the creation and refinement of design systems.&lt;SEP&gt;An agent identified by the name "ux-designer" using the Opus model, focused on interface design, visual polish, usability, and responsive design, with expertise in shadcn/ui and Tailwind CSS, and adhering to Anti-AI-slop design principles.&lt;SEP&gt;A specialized agent with a focus on interface design, visual polish, usability, and responsive design, added to the Coding Team.&lt;SEP&gt;A specialized agent with a focus on interface design, visual polish, usability, and responsive design, added to the Coding Team.&lt;SEP&gt;A specialized agent with a focus on interface design, visual polish, usability, and responsive design, added to the Coding Team.&lt;SEP&gt;A specialized agent with a focus on interface design, visual polish, usability, and responsive design, added to the Coding Team.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d395d729f7f4af176337bfefc3a79dd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c9f0047cf0851b406258ad13a0ecf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb41aa2ca304e58f55fd006f67adb483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d310a4043708aa267f31226740ed083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b037432a7b9144971fd46cf952d906de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fee19755a3251618ba78c3efffeb833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22dff12fa45dfc4789663451e530bd72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-876c9d36604a2a00ba9d1acc186c490c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4a759f0caa83cf9e50057d50a49419</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772910489</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interface Design">
  <data key="d0">Interface Design</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Interface Design is identified as a significant focus area for the UX/UI Designer Agent. Multiple descriptions emphasize its importance, labeling it as a primary, key, and core area of focus. Furthermore, it is highlighted as a specific area of expertise for this agent, indicating its central role in their professional domain.&lt;SEP&gt;Interface design is a focus area for the Ux-Designer agent.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d395d729f7f4af176337bfefc3a79dd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c9f0047cf0851b406258ad13a0ecf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb41aa2ca304e58f55fd006f67adb483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d310a4043708aa267f31226740ed083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b037432a7b9144971fd46cf952d906de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22dff12fa45dfc4789663451e530bd72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-876c9d36604a2a00ba9d1acc186c490c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b4a759f0caa83cf9e50057d50a49419&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37056b34934d569bff0b96c6e8991103</data>
