<node id="Long-Horizon Thinking">
  <data key="d0">Long-Horizon Thinking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Long-Horizon Thinking is a key theme consistently identified for a white paper. This white paper is specifically developed for an Executive Strategic Development Class and focuses on exploring why executives should engage with literature. The concept of Long-Horizon Thinking itself highlights a strategic mindset that emphasizes the careful consideration of long-term implications and future outcomes in decision-making.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-Horizon Thinking is a key theme of the white paper, presented as a benefit of reading literature.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-Horizon Thinking is a key theme for executives discussed in the white paper document.&lt;SEP&gt;A key theme for the white paper, emphasizing the importance of planning and foresight over extended periods.&lt;SEP&gt;Long-Horizon Thinking is a key theme promoted in the White Paper For Executives as a benefit of reading literature.</data>
