<node id="Claude Opus 4-6">
  <data key="d0">Claude Opus 4-6</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Claude Opus 4-6 is a newly released and specific version of the Claude Opus AI model, developed by Anthropic. Identified by the designation `anthropic/claude-opus-4-6`, this model was set as a primary AI model, serving as an update from the previous Opus-4-5 version.

This particular iteration of the Claude Opus model was utilized both as a central primary model and for managing associated systems. It was specifically employed to update sub-agents, with records indicating it was used to update 28 Opus sub-agents. Notably, during its deployment, Claude Opus 4-6 initially failed but subsequently became operational after a retry. An individual or entity named Anirach is documented to have switched to and updated sub-agents with this model.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific version of the Claude Opus AI model, used as a primary model and for sub-agents.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific version of the Claude Opus AI model, used as a primary model and for sub-agents.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific version of the Claude Opus AI model, used as a primary model and for sub-agents.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific version of the Claude Opus AI model, used as a primary model and for sub-agents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bfd74135092e0a76db2ea1ed4d25f626&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cee8abd51a4604f1cb2cd2d460b6adae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71616aeafc61b899b58cf170dee71ae7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d3bd213694bc9e9a86ea3a0c974c0d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67b1aad64c74e49b536dcee4842fd95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e907075cce78e0ea06d5e60daafa4c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cfc6c6d57918fbe9483abfa3d8a7110&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eedf5e93d60ec2ab2ee6bc42ed024f3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772910258</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
