<node id="FastAPI">
  <data key="d0">FastAPI</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">FastAPI is a Python web framework designed for building APIs. It is frequently employed for creating backend API routes, enabling connectivity with frontend frameworks such as Next.js. In the specific context of ChartSense AI, FastAPI functions as a key backend framework, facilitating the interaction with the Next.js frontend and its API routes. This technology is a crucial component in the development of the ChartSense AI Minimum Viable Product (MVP).

Furthermore, FastAPI is recognized and indexed within various knowledge management systems. It is listed as a topic in the Knowledge Graph, appears in the Obsidian topic index, and is specifically identified as an entry within the KnowledgeGraph/Topics index.&lt;SEP&gt;A web framework used in the project's tech stack.&lt;SEP&gt;FastAPI is a technology or framework related to the ChartSense AI project.&lt;SEP&gt;A web framework mentioned as a technology for badges and backend setup.&lt;SEP&gt;FastAPI is a Python web framework used for building the project's backend APIs.&lt;SEP&gt;A technology used in the ChartSense AI MVP stack.</data>
