<node id="Translation Philosophy">
  <data key="d0">Translation Philosophy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Translation Philosophy is a person associated with a knowledge graph entry and translation activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Guiding principles for the Thai translation, emphasizing natural Thai prose, cultural adaptation, modern style, and justified formatting.&lt;SEP&gt;The core principles guiding the Translation Team's approach to translation.&lt;SEP&gt;The guiding principle for the translation, which is to make the Thai text feel like it was originally written in Thai.&lt;SEP&gt;Translation Philosophy is the guiding principle that aims to make translated text feel originally written in the target language.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e2a5f7ec66752e21d47da4c856ee6a27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ac42e4b444b2aa35a9817c58b1eaadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-734ec6fc710d1be198572ead525f9006&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba508f45949882ad8abe499c098ae8d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d047eaf54d53203dc7bc212b545fea70</data>
