<node id="Quality Gates">
  <data key="d0">Quality Gates</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Quality Gates are a set of criteria, checks, or checkpoints implemented at various stages of a process to ensure quality. These gates have been incorporated into team workflows and are now included in every team guide, often resulting from initiatives like the Collaboration Workflows Project.

Their fundamental purpose is to ensure that specific quality standards are met throughout a process and before any final delivery. For example, in book production, Quality Gates are applied at distinct stages such as Outline, Research, Draft, Dev Edit, Copy Edit, and Final. Adherence to these criteria is mandatory before a book is delivered, such as to Google Drive. More broadly, they represent a necessary set of checks that must be passed before any product or deliverable is released.

In certain technical contexts, Quality Gates are implemented as automated pre-PR (Pull Request) checks, which may include validations for build, linting, testing, security, and bundling. This serves as a new capability within collaboration workflows to enforce quality at each stage.&lt;SEP&gt;Checks within team workflows powered by skills.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98ee600c3aaf8c0514fc103e242dc4e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b5ee91f5b0653fb208892bb9c89c90a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f0b1ecc0f7298380d9a5583da3c7fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46acd3e509aa2a1265a39d2c0a5e6f5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c054e84c33d3f105219dae9aad1c8a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82bb69ddf92ab1babcdff33347dda2cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b394110aeea60586b9d87bbb1349ec3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37056b34934d569bff0b96c6e8991103&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9e9ea9f9ef3e6e49b68f230ad0b56ef</data>
