<node id="Node.js">
  <data key="d0">Node.js</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Node.js is a JavaScript runtime environment that serves as a fundamental technology across various applications and projects.

It is specifically utilized in the Team Manuals V4 project for the generation of manuals. Node.js also provides the operational environment for PptxGenJS 4.0.1 and is identified as a technology instrumental for badges and frontend setup. Additionally, it is essential for DOCX generation.

The runtime environment, with version 22 specifically, is newly supported by an upgraded Docker image. It is notable that Node.js is not accessible from sub-agent sandboxes, which impacts functionalities such as DOCX generation within those constrained environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4cb2da7ce21279bc4524ae53da55f5f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ba71d5d5bc8db56c16d1e6b194a9f03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-115813a810d0017b7b8bfde9c5b23920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c073468c56d6856982b9f7b826195bd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2b262e13581f7379dcb10606742e711&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-000e5cbc3c5b62de4af4981edce03d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-631efd939c35e0e48c213128b1245c1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9e9ea9f9ef3e6e49b68f230ad0b56ef</data>
