<node id="Batch Event">
  <data key="d0">Batch Event</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A Batch Event is defined as a recurring scheduled process or processing event. This type of event is consistently documented with various timestamps, and its origin often traces back to specific data sources. A primary function of a Batch Event is to update various components within a knowledge graph, and it also serves to record daily activities or session snapshots.&lt;SEP&gt;A recurring scheduled process, documented with various timestamps, often originating from specific data sources.&lt;SEP&gt;A Batch Event is a recurring processing event that updates various knowledge graph components and records daily activities or session snapshots.</data>
