  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Anong is characterized as a nostalgic storyteller, a prominent figure in the Thai Version Storyline of "Three Old Men: The Last Conversation." Within this narrative, Anong holds the distinction of being the oldest character, approximately 85 years old.

His personal history reveals a background linked to the ownership of 17 fishing boats, and he is noted to have had a deceased wife named Noi. A distinctive feature of Anong's presence in the story is that all of his interactions are systematically logged by the Memory Log.&lt;SEP&gt;A nostalgic storyteller whose interactions are logged by Memory Log.&lt;SEP&gt;A person identified as a "nostalgic storyteller."&lt;SEP&gt;Anong is a nostalgic storyteller.</data>
