<node id="Agent:Chapter-Writer:Main Session">
  <data key="d0">Agent:Chapter-Writer:Main Session</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An Agent:Chapter-Writer:Main Session is a specific, active, operational, and named system session. It is distinctly identified by the unique identifier "agent:chapter-writer:main". This session is managed by an agent, which is itself identified as 'chapter-writer:main'. A key characteristic of an Agent:Chapter-Writer:Main Session is its association with snapshots, serving as the direct source from which these snapshots are taken. Furthermore, this session is also actively associated with various messages.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific active session identified by "agent:chapter-writer:main", which is associated with snapshots and messages.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific operational session of an agent, from which a snapshot was taken.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific active session identified by "agent:chapter-writer:main", which is associated with snapshots and messages.</data>
