<node id="Memory Search Fix">
  <data key="d0">Memory Search Fix</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Memory Search Fix is a specific corrective action applied during system optimization sessions. This fix is primarily designed to address and resolve issues related to memory search functionality. In addition to memory search, the Memory Search Fix also targets and resolves problems associated with the Google embedding provider. The specific action taken by this fix involves changing or correcting the `baseUrl` for the Google Embedding Provider.</data>
