<node id="Pre-Compaction Summary">
  <data key="d0">Pre-Compaction Summary</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A Pre-Compaction Summary is a specialized summary or section within session notes that serves to capture critical key state information. This summary is specifically generated and recorded prior to a compaction process, effectively documenting the state before such an operation takes place. It often encompasses and details extensive work conducted across multiple projects, consolidating relevant information into a cohesive overview. Beyond merely capturing the key state, this summary can also function as a flush trigger, indicating a significant point or action within a session, particularly during summary compaction.&lt;SEP&gt;A summary capturing key state information before a compaction process.</data>
