<node id="Database">
  <data key="d0">Database</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Database is an organized and structured collection of information or data, typically residing within the Data Layer of a larger system. It functions as the underlying repository for various data tables, which can include entities such as activities, users, teams, deal_logs, and pipelines, all designed to be efficiently queried for data retrieval and manipulation.

Beyond its role as a data store, 'Database' also refers to comprehensive management practices. These encompass the administration of schemas, the execution of data migrations, and ongoing optimization efforts, which are often a core focus area for a DB-Specialist. In a technical or development context, 'Database' can also specify the particular database technology that is either implemented or required for a specific Development Environment.

Furthermore, the term 'Database' is widely utilized as a categorical tag or concept. When tagged in documentation like the 'VPIPE Database Query Guide,' it indicates that the content's subject matter pertains to databases in general, signifying a broader discussion or reference to database principles and applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-558068083b50e64390babf7d3bc77da7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7ea538b28ba259f1e19bcce7655c6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42b2d817f88febf88e53eafe461680f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d4fc739af34749a77835c444863b904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ebea4e6d0303f5cfa3e72df0eb20ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12a77499fd86767b7b2628b024b4cadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd423fd12ecb6cccdd6c05c4eee67a81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f3170cda74e372e7eaa1a8a5e32e553</data>
