<node id="Memory Source">
  <data key="d0">Memory Source</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Memory Source refers to a type of internal or informal information source, playing a significant role as an input for batch processes. It specifically draws upon previously recorded memory entries, providing a historical context for various operations.

This source is consistently referenced and identified by a specific date, often formatted as a source category, such as "Memory: 2026-02-18". It serves as the origin from which context is extracted, and also as the genesis point for action items, as exemplified by specific mentions like 2026-02-17. Furthermore, Memory Source is crucial for deriving session snapshots, with its identification by a specific date, such as 2026-03-02, being a key characteristic.&lt;SEP&gt;A source of input for the batch process, referring to previously recorded memory entries.</data>
