<node id="Session">
  <data key="d0">Session</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Session represents an interactive context or period of activity, intrinsically associated with an agent and messages exchanged within that context. It is understood as an active interactive process, capable of being specifically identified, such as `agent:chapter-writer:main`.

Each Session functions as a recorded interaction or conversation, uniquely identified and occurring at a specific point in time. This period of activity is also subject to analysis, often by specialized tools like the Session Learning Miner.

Furthermore, a Session can manifest as a work period, encompassing extensive work across multiple projects, involving context loading, and potentially serving as a flush trigger. Examples of such work sessions include one that occurred on February 23, 2026, and another on March 2, 2026.&lt;SEP&gt;A Session represents an interactive context or period of activity, associated with an agent and messages.&lt;SEP&gt;An active interactive process, specifically identified as `agent:chapter-writer:main`, during which messages are exchanged.&lt;SEP&gt;A Session represents an interactive context or period of activity, associated with an agent and messages.&lt;SEP&gt;An active interactive process, specifically identified as `agent:chapter-writer:main`, during which messages are exchanged.</data>
