<node id="Decision Document">
  <data key="d0">Decision Document</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A Decision Document is a markdown file primarily used to formally record and document specific decisions made within a project or system. These documents are typically located within the `KnowledgeGraph/Decisions/` directory, following a consistent naming convention that often includes a date and a descriptive title, such as `2026-02-17-Filter-won-deals-by-close_datetime-NOT-create_datetime.md` or `2026-02-18-NCD-CIE-validation-must-be-reframed--synthetic--sanity-check-NHANES-concordance-.md`. Another example is the file `2026-02-22-Always-spawn-sub-agents-for-tasks-longer-than-30-seconds.md`, which also serves this purpose.

The scope of decisions recorded by a Decision Document is broad, covering various technical and architectural choices. Examples include the decision to use SQLite for local development, the method for filtering won deals by `close_datetime` rather than `create_datetime`, or the choice to increase the compaction buffer. Other documented decisions pertain to reframing NCD CIE validation for synthetic sanity checks and NHANES concordance, defining rules for spawning sub-agents for tasks exceeding 30 seconds, or specifying the PPTX format for slide generation. Additionally, decisions like performing DOCX generation from the main session due to sub-agent limitations, as recorded on 2026-02-16, and those made via `information_schema` queries, are also captured in these dedicated markdown files.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f070dc633489f685a59e40392fc9154a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd0ccd8a9f7a8658474ff41f4568f053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf917e9d32da670c5b288b96f6ec512f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00b881fac5d94f295a6236193fad4f91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15c956d1b8aee7ee1ab799cb4d8b6fa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2512a1902cdc7b135fa04c725a1649d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82737226bf4c5bc8eb7724d162c70efb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e44677d3b7901dfac79e002aeb0d11a5</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1772825133</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Obsidian: Daily/2026-02-10.md">
  <data key="d0">Obsidian: Daily/2026-02-10.md</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
