<node id="Action Item Type">
  <data key="d0">Action Item Type</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Action Item Type refers to a fundamental classification or categorization used to designate an entity, such as an item, document, or task, as an "action item." This type explicitly defines the nature of the described object, indicating that it requires specific action or follow-up. It acts as a category or label, often specified through metadata like 'type' or 'tags', which clarifies that the item is a task necessitating resolution or execution.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification or category indicating that an item is an actionable task.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification indicating that the item is an action item, derived from the metadata.&lt;SEP&gt;Action Item Type is a classification for tasks or pieces of work that need to be done.</data>
