<node id="Asia/Bangkok">
  <data key="d0">Asia/Bangkok</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Asia/Bangkok refers to a specific time zone, identified as UTC+07:00, which serves as the chronological reference point for various logging events and activities within an operational system. This timezone is where logging events occur, such as a specific instance at 23:30.

It is the designated timezone from which work logs are officially recorded, logged, and generated, ensuring their chronological accuracy. Asia/Bangkok is also the operational base for the agent logging system. Specifically, the Chapter-Writer cron logs its activities and events from this timezone, including the chronological recording of the Course Team Work Log.&lt;SEP&gt;Asia/Bangkok is the updated time zone setting for the clock on the LobsterBoard Dashboard.&lt;SEP&gt;A user timezone setting applied in configuration changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aedfee7ce4f9e7f83127a2422080d7b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa5f3a0dec5b20e14cc7cc2015e60c99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ff3f0f5d285d27b8ba97f792fba560e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-235bc07c09f26fdcb46115a35a1fb596&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b2d7eca9e5caaa2ebab4c11d5b308eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-000e5cbc3c5b62de4af4981edce03d36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d713004e53905bc9678b48a899d29a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ced3e03077dc272a4034f7f14b2b7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffed2e0d5a98ce8d9cb5106e19cdcce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1d361334741e195fd3cc01498c5d61d</data>
