</edge>
<edge source="Knowledge Graph" target="Obsidian">
  <data key="d7">60.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Knowledge Graph and Obsidian describes Obsidian as a prominent software application and comprehensive knowledge management system. Obsidian is specifically engineered to implement, manage, and host a Knowledge Graph, providing the essential infrastructure and specialized tools necessary for its maintenance and ongoing user engagement. It serves as the central platform where users actively manage, organize, and interact with the content contained within a Knowledge Graph, encompassing general content, files, specific documents, person profiles, reference documents, and other detailed information. Obsidian handles the underlying file structure and overall content storage, often indicated by its association with Knowledge Graph file paths and tags, and is frequently identified as the primary source for Knowledge Graph content.

Beyond its function as a platform for external Knowledge Graphs, Obsidian also leverages the Knowledge Graph methodology for organizing its internal knowledge base. It structures its own information and connections through this graph-based approach, effectively using a Knowledge Graph to organize its content and internal knowledge. Therefore, Obsidian's knowledge base and content are inherently structured and organized using a Knowledge Graph.&lt;SEP&gt;Obsidian is a software application that implements and manages a Knowledge Graph.&lt;SEP&gt;Obsidian acts as the platform for the Knowledge Graph.&lt;SEP&gt;Obsidian is the platform that manages and implements the Knowledge Graph.</data>
  <data key="d9">application,architecture,contains,content organization,context,host,hosting,hosts,implements,location,management,manages,manages components of,manages information,operates,organization,organizes,platform,platform for,related to,source,structure,system,system integration,tool,tool for,tool usage,tool used</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-02c142cb55bfe21786326d82ec655339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e064beaa9addbc9ee14f687e59311381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ada2e9500cf083516501a8b590959545&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de7d2b034444ef30c5cd263afdaf88fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-209a10793a38ab9ffb1236b426b5f37a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa0b04516491978cd7f2fd3497bd74a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f30a8d91993f68af9395b1e286ae615&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d6c77d7d3fec1f1b3a7f55eae6a5362&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b305d4fb2e0053a2c1d60fafeff74829&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505a6de49a4e71323e53e984bc770e7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88e992b721430779160720a86027f0b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a764628ee2a0d96bcbab465f3adff1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dfb21adb069bd3559c2ef99603a326a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48404c33a0cecaca96752c576cc8ff1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9c462842e032fe02bd3a26f0182a79d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e3f7a26a4c8d639a7927de46537f385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d38a9ea2781994983d82c56aaf21d90c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b839046231fcd4f0b3dcf5aa7e6c1490&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6201337fe894c42a726729fd7b3d568a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2247baf68504edcbb686f816523e53e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1b781e3e1d8f6931cf3aac3e89a4627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36bc7aa9b32e316be7bff4a8f43fad50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16405385759a81e20e5b226bbba714cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb209bf42350b9e170471b4f0b4d8f51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34d9ec198ae427665d14d305ed714134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-740c826e0488c9c7d4bb49a2bc4b77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a36fcfa3f0abcaf5629e5ecad38f0cb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f9a385ebc3487ab67289add07185a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b61ade4889db4f6a01bf96731f64a7c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-204b0227c0c120113918139adb369e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c48e9d5ad18db20533f0ce8ce25701b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f85fe68f46c78a79e02f9705ab0304e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ee70ff66b5db6fafbda166046803fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8cba83ad815daf324fb66f8121ca897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff940504f8d9447b54a694d9aa350b45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09744a76a69ed9486ce7b280dd884b0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5f174664d1cea2b5dff02b5d7d0e6a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3ae39579d8b764c6c813b3be381abe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d31c18aa7d1cfcb501caaac74699be0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bad9fb1e5163e6414596ae7be5069a0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-869e83062a212366