<edge source="Obsidian" target="KnowledgeGraph">
  <data key="d7">19.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Obsidian is a software tool and platform that plays a comprehensive role in the management and implementation of the KnowledgeGraph. It functions as the application where various aspects of the KnowledgeGraph are contained, hosted, and organized, effectively serving as the primary platform for storing and managing its information and content.

Specifically, Obsidian is responsible for managing the KnowledgeGraph's overall structure, including its files and its index. It implements the KnowledgeGraph system and organizes its content, providing the interface for managing and interacting with the KnowledgeGraph. Furthermore, Obsidian is integral to the KnowledgeGraph structure, particularly within its "Topics" category, where it aids in organization and management. The KnowledgeGraph system is thus managed, accessed, and stored within the Obsidian platform.&lt;SEP&gt;Obsidian is used to manage content structured as a KnowledgeGraph.&lt;SEP&gt;Obsidian is the platform where the KnowledgeGraph content is stored.&lt;SEP&gt;Obsidian is used as a tool for managing components or aspects of a knowledge graph, as indicated by the file paths.&lt;SEP&gt;Obsidian is a system that contains and manages the KnowledgeGraph component.</data>
