<edge source="Knowledge Graph Index" target="People Category">
  <data key="d7">61.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation "(Knowledge Graph Index, People Category)" defines the comprehensive manner in which the Knowledge Graph Index (KGI) integrates, presents, and manages information related to the People Category. This signifies that the KGI fundamentally encompasses and incorporates the People Category as a core component of its overall structure and content.

The KGI is responsible for effectively categorizing entries and content within this domain, specifically including and organizing information pertaining to individuals and items under the People Category. It categorizes various entries under this classification, providing a thorough overview and integrating associated data.

Furthermore, the Knowledge Graph Index offers quantitative and statistical insights into the People Category. It tracks and contains the People Category, providing both detailed and aggregate counts for all entries classified under it. For instance, the KGI reports a precise count of entries for the People Category, such as 315, which represents the number of individuals or items related to "People" within the index, thereby offering an overview of the People Category count. In essence, the KGI includes, categorizes, and provides statistical insights into the People Category and its associated entries.&lt;SEP&gt;The Knowledge Graph Index includes the People Category.</data>
