<edge source="Knowledge Graph Index" target="Decisions Category">
  <data key="d7">61.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation "(Decisions Category, Knowledge Graph Index)" defines the comprehensive method by which the Knowledge Graph Index presents, organizes, and classifies information pertaining to the Decisions Category. It serves as the central mechanism for content classification, fully encompassing, tracking, and managing the Decisions Category as one of its particular classifications.

In its role, the Knowledge Graph Index is responsible for categorizing various entries, items, and content under the Decisions Category. It provides an overview that details all relevant data related to this category, along with a specific aggregate count of its entries or content. This aggregate count offers a clear, quantifiable measure of the Decisions Category's scope and presence, consistently noted to include 6 entries. Through these functions, the Knowledge Graph Index elaborates on the content of the Decisions Category and provides measurable insights.&lt;SEP&gt;The Knowledge Graph Index includes the Decisions Category.</data>
