<edge source="Knowledge Graph Index" target="Decisions Count">
  <data key="d7">18.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (Decisions Count, Knowledge Graph Index) describes the mechanism through which the Knowledge Graph Index records and presents information regarding the number of decisions. The Knowledge Graph Index consistently provides an overview that includes a count of these decisions, often referred to as the "Decisions Count." This count functions as a specific numerical data point within the index.

The Knowledge Graph Index includes a count for the "Decisions" category, presenting this as an overview. In some contexts, this overview count for decisions is explicitly stated as 6 decisions, highlighting its role in providing precise numerical data regarding the decisions it indexes. It effectively records and features the Decisions Count as a distinct category.&lt;SEP&gt;The Knowledge Graph Index provides an overview that includes the count of 6 decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Knowledge Graph Index records the Decisions Count.&lt;SEP&gt;The Knowledge Graph Index provides a count of "Decisions".</data>
  <data key="d9">categorization,category,contains,includes,measures,metric,overview,tracks</data>
