  <data key="d8">The relation between Google Embedding Provider and Memory Search signifies a fundamental association where Memory Search functionality directly relies on and utilizes the Google Embedding Provider as a core component for its operations. This indicates a direct dependency, with Memory Search leveraging the Google Embedding Provider to function.

A specific characteristic of the Google Embedding Provider's role in this relationship was that its configuration was fixed. Despite this, Memory Search functionality encountered issues tied to the Google Embedding Provider. These issues specifically included a general configuration problem and a more precise `baseUrl` issue, which directly impacted the Memory Search functionality. Ultimately, the issues affecting Memory Search were resolved by correcting the `baseUrl` of the Google Embedding Provider.&lt;SEP&gt;The issue with Memory Search was related to the Google Embedding Provider.&lt;SEP&gt;The Memory Search functionality was impacted by a `baseUrl` issue originating from the Google Embedding Provider.&lt;SEP&gt;Memory Search relies on the Google Embedding Provider, whose configuration was fixed.&lt;SEP&gt;The Memory Search functionality uses the Google Embedding Provider.</data>
