<edge source="BKK" target="Session Snapshot">
  <data key="d7">17.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation (BKK, Session Snapshot) indicates that a Session Snapshot is recorded with a time reference or timestamp that is specifically associated with BKK. This means the Session Snapshot's time is specified within the location context of BKK, explicitly referencing the BKK timezone and its geographic location, Bangkok.

For example, a Session Snapshot event might be recorded with a timestamp such as 09:31, where this time is unequivocally attributed to the BKK timezone. The Session Snapshot is thus understood to have been taken or recorded at a time associated with the BKK location, ensuring its timestamp is interpreted according to Bangkok time.&lt;SEP&gt;The Session Snapshot was taken at a time associated with the BKK location.&lt;SEP&gt;The Session Snapshot is recorded with a time reference in BKK (Bangkok).</data>
  <data key="d9">location,location context,occurred at,recording,time context,time reference,timed at,timestamp,timestamp context,timestamp location</data>
