<edge source="Daily Notes" target="Memory">
  <data key="d7">15.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Daily Notes and Memory describes Memory as the designated source system for Daily Notes. Memory functions as the storage location where Daily Notes are kept and contained.

This implies that Daily Notes, which may document various sessions and events, are retrieved directly from Memory. For instance, Daily Notes for specific dates, such as March 1, 2026, are sourced from and stored within Memory. Thus, Memory acts as both the origin and the persistent repository for all Daily Notes.&lt;SEP&gt;Daily Notes are sourced from Memory.&lt;SEP&gt;Memory acts as a source that stores Daily Notes, documenting various sessions and events.&lt;SEP&gt;Memory is the source system that provides the Daily Notes.&lt;SEP&gt;Memory contains Daily Notes.&lt;SEP&gt;Memory is the source system that provides the Daily Notes.&lt;SEP&gt;Memory contains Daily Notes.</data>
