All provided descriptions uniformly state that "Session Notes" contain or address a "Pre-Compaction Summary," often highlighting the terms with quotation marks, which may imply they are specific sections, document types, or named components within a larger structure. The consensus across all sources reinforces that the "Pre-Compaction Summary" forms a constituent element or a referenced body of work within the "Session Notes."&lt;SEP&gt;Session Notes include a pre-compaction summary.</data>
