<edge source="Database Schema" target="Book Model">
  <data key="d7">12.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between a Book Model and a Database Schema describes a structural definition. The Database Schema for a project encompasses and defines the Book Model, meaning the Book Model is an integral component specified within the database schema. This establishes that the Database Schema includes and outlines the structure and characteristics of the Book Model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines a Book Model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines a Book Model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines a Book Model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines a Book Model.</data>
  <data key="d9">component,data structure,defines,includes,includes model</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-33c82f85cdf1f3f6b459569c71f52f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71616aeafc61b899b58cf170dee71ae7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7f38dc891390630b7d242b504ad3d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa45fc280386a72b3dcb6042866c05f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27eb544ea04492b03b59296d1e3b207f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6bf94f806b19bcd3c3ef94a2f41033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563e9b5c607a87d47046fea356d51100&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c771a2e8e4cd46c72a573a9ec2caf7c6</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1772910302</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Database Schema" target="Author Model">
  <data key="d7">12.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation "(Author Model, Database Schema)" signifies that the Database Schema is responsible for defining and incorporating the Author Model. The Author Model exists as a fundamental component or structure within the broader Database Schema.

This indicates that the Database Schema outlines and includes the specifications for the Author Model, making it an integral part of a project's overall database architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines an Author Model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines an Author Model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines an Author Model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines an Author Model.</data>
  <data key="d9">component,data structure,defines,includes,includes model</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-33c82f85cdf1f3f6b459569c71f52f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71616aeafc61b899b58cf170dee71ae7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7f38dc891390630b7d242b504ad3d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa45fc280386a72b3dcb6042866c05f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27eb544ea04492b03b59296d1e3b207f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d6bf94f806b19bcd3c3ef94a2f41033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-563e9b5c607a87d47046fea356d51100&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c771a2e8e4cd46c72a573a9ec2caf7c6</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1772910303</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Database Schema" target="Genre Model">
  <data key="d7">12.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between a Database Schema and a Genre Model signifies that the Database Schema encompasses and defines the structure of the Genre Model. This means the Genre Model is an integral component that is specified and included within the overall Database Schema. In various implementations, this Database Schema may be specific to a particular project.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines a Genre Model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines a Genre Model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines a Genre Model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Database Schema defines a Genre Model.</data>
  <data key="d9">component,data structure,defines,includes,includes model</data>
