  <data key="d8">The relation between an Action Item and an Action Item Document indicates that the Action Item Document serves as the comprehensive descriptor and repository for the Action Item. This document is responsible for formally detailing, documenting, and providing all necessary context for a given Action Item, effectively containing its specifics.

The Action Item Document itself is specifically categorized and identified through its attributes. It is explicitly defined as being of the type 'action-item' and is consistently tagged as an 'action-item'. For instance, an action item concerning a script timeout would find its full documentation within this particular type of file, the Action Item Document.</data>
  <data key="d9">categorization,classification,contained in,contains,describes,details,documented by,documented in,documents,tagging,type</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-4921daf2164de8d78817ea40ef7438fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2bfbe87d5ce5fcc4ebe045a23d0c8bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abf907c5e36499f7a4ccbff7a18a5031&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-614be20b6b5d9a223ad1f1221a3397aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-564d8cbe6d4c74180f4e5a59066a30ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed97bca06c7f4723df0597a679b6d4f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-871d601ea0724a2ba77ac39328982ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f61537e834b72ab7e7890749912feb</data>
